1
00:00:23,172 --> 00:00:25,882
Things are never gonna
be the same now.

2
00:00:26,252 --> 00:00:27,572
I mean, look at this.

3
00:00:28,242 --> 00:00:29,242
We got aliens.

4
00:00:30,502 --> 00:00:33,672
We got big green guys
tearing down buildings.

5
00:00:34,032 --> 00:00:37,142
When I was a kid I used to
draw cowboys and Indians.

6
00:00:37,242 --> 00:00:39,242
Actually,
it's Native American, but...

7
00:00:41,222 --> 00:00:42,732
Yeah,
tell you what, though...

8
00:00:43,929 --> 00:00:45,329
Not bad, is it?

9
00:00:46,692 --> 00:00:49,622
No, yeah.
Kid's got a future.

10
00:00:50,232 --> 00:00:52,232
Yeah, well...

11
00:00:52,702 --> 00:00:54,102
We'll see, I guess.

12
00:01:18,052 --> 00:01:19,492
No, hey...

13
00:01:19,903 --> 00:01:22,058
You can't saw through that stuff.

14
00:01:22,482 --> 00:01:26,682
These alien bastards are tough.
You gotta use the stuff they use.

15
00:01:28,792 --> 00:01:30,792
- See? All right.
- All right.

16
00:01:33,014 --> 00:01:34,014
Oh, Hey..

17
00:01:35,192 --> 00:01:37,272
Glad you could join us.
Afternoon.

18
00:01:37,272 --> 00:01:40,012
- My alarm's been going off...
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. Your alarm.

19
00:01:40,052 --> 00:01:42,742
Look, just go stock
that armor plating like I asked.

20
00:01:42,742 --> 00:01:44,408
This is a huge deal for us.

21
00:01:44,432 --> 00:01:48,912
Attention, please. In accordance
with Executive order 396-B...

22
00:01:49,172 --> 00:01:52,632
All post battle cleanup operations
are now under our jurisdiction.

23
00:01:52,642 --> 00:01:55,112
Thank you for your service.
We'll take it from here.

24
00:01:55,112 --> 00:01:57,842
- Who the hell are you?
- Qualified personnel.

25
00:01:57,872 --> 00:02:02,192
Look, I have a city contract, to salvage
all this, okay? With the city, so...

26
00:02:02,192 --> 00:02:06,712
I apologize, Mr. Toomes. But all salvage
operations are now under our jurisdiction.

27
00:02:06,792 --> 00:02:10,132
Please turn over any and all exotic
materials that you've collected,

28
00:02:10,132 --> 00:02:13,042
- or you will be prosecuted.
- Ma'am, what are....

29
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:15,842
Please, wait up, come on.

30
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:20,342
- I can lose my house!
- I'm sorry, sir. There's nothing I can do.

31
00:02:21,852 --> 00:02:23,952
Maybe next time,
don't overextend yourself.

32
00:02:25,892 --> 00:02:27,892
What'd you say?

33
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:33,582
Yeah. He's right.
I overextended myself.

34
00:02:36,872 --> 00:02:38,872
Put them down.

35
00:02:40,592 --> 00:02:43,202
If you have a grievance,
you may take it up with my superiors.

36
00:02:43,862 --> 00:02:46,092
Your superiors?
Who the hell are they?!

37
00:02:46,092 --> 00:02:48,602
<font color="#ffff00"><i>The joint venture between Stark
Industries and the federal government,</i></font>

38
00:02:48,642 --> 00:02:50,773
<font color="#ffff00"><i>the Department of DAMAGE CONTROL,</i></font>

39
00:02:50,798 --> 00:02:54,798
<font color="#ffff00"><i>will oversee the collection and storage
of alien and other exotic materials.</i></font>

40
00:02:54,872 --> 00:02:57,572
So now the assholes who made this
mess are getting paid to clean it up?

41
00:02:58,042 --> 00:03:01,423
- Yeah, it's all rigged.
<i><font color="#ffff00">- Experts estimate there are over 1,500 tons...</font></i>

42
00:03:01,448 --> 00:03:05,072
<font color="#ffff00"><i>...of exotic materials
scattered throughout the Tristate area.</i></font>

43
00:03:05,072 --> 00:03:09,112
Hey, Chief, we still have
another load from yesterday.

44
00:03:09,262 --> 00:03:11,612
- We're supposed to turn this in, right?
- I ain't hauling it.

45
00:03:11,612 --> 00:03:16,112
It's too bad. We could've made some
pretty cool stuff from all that alien junk.

46
00:03:18,052 --> 00:03:21,952
I tell you what. Let's keep it.

47
00:03:23,432 --> 00:03:25,432
The world's changing.

48
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:31,042
It's time we change, too.

49
00:03:31,588 --> 00:03:33,788
<font color="#ffff00">8 YEARS LATER</font>

50
00:04:15,072 --> 00:04:17,072
Here you go, Mason.

51
00:04:21,112 --> 00:04:23,112
Business is good.

52
00:04:59,153 --> 00:05:02,017
<font color="#ffff00">a Film by Peter Parker</font>

53
00:05:02,772 --> 00:05:04,572
New York, Queens.

54
00:05:04,602 --> 00:05:06,692
It's a rough borough,
but hey, it's home.

55
00:05:06,692 --> 00:05:09,402
- Who are you talking to?
- No one.

56
00:05:09,402 --> 00:05:12,649
- Just making a little video of the trip.
- You know you can't show it to anyone.

57
00:05:12,674 --> 00:05:14,832
- Yeah, I know.
- Then why are you narrating in that voice?

58
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:18,198
- Hmm. Because it's fun.
- "Fun".

59
00:05:18,222 --> 00:05:20,552
So, uhh, why do they call you "Happy"?

60
00:05:23,752 --> 00:05:26,272
Come on. I'm not carrying your bags.
Let's go.

61
00:05:26,592 --> 00:05:29,062
Hey, should I go to
the bathroom before?

62
00:05:29,062 --> 00:05:32,512
- There's a bathroom on it.
- Woah, no pilot? That's awesome!

63
00:05:33,252 --> 00:05:35,272
- Is that where you're gonna sit?
- Yeah.

64
00:05:35,272 --> 00:05:38,928
- Is it your first time on a private plane?
- It's my first time on any plane.

65
00:05:38,952 --> 00:05:40,952
Should it be making that noise?

66
00:05:51,352 --> 00:05:55,472
No one has actually told me why
I'm in Berlin. Or what I'm doing.

67
00:05:55,472 --> 00:05:58,952
Something about,
Captain America going crazy...

68
00:05:58,952 --> 00:06:01,032
- This is you.
- Oh, we're neighbors?

69
00:06:01,072 --> 00:06:03,112
We're not roommates. Suit up.

70
00:06:03,122 --> 00:06:05,432
- Okay, Peter. You got this.
- What the hell are you wearing?

71
00:06:07,032 --> 00:06:09,332
- It's my suit.
- Where's the case?

72
00:06:09,712 --> 00:06:10,652
What case?

73
00:06:10,752 --> 00:06:13,352
That's not my what? I thought that was a closet.
This is still my room?

74
00:06:13,352 --> 00:06:15,448
My room is way bigger than I...

75
00:06:15,472 --> 00:06:17,552
Hey, I found the case.

76
00:06:18,392 --> 00:06:20,392
"A minor upgrade"?

77
00:06:20,422 --> 00:06:23,022
Woah! Oh, my God!

78
00:06:23,862 --> 00:06:25,048
Put it on.

79
00:06:25,372 --> 00:06:27,372
This is the coolest
thing I've ever seen, ever!

80
00:06:27,372 --> 00:06:31,282
- Let's go!
- But, I don't understand, is it for me?

81
00:06:31,382 --> 00:06:33,382
Happy, Happy, wait!

82
00:06:33,502 --> 00:06:37,098
This is insane! Insane! Look
at this thing! Look at the eyes!

83
00:06:37,922 --> 00:06:39,922
- This is the greatest day of my life.
- Let's go.

84
00:06:40,752 --> 00:06:43,392
Okay. There's Captain America,
 Iron Man, Black Widow...

85
00:06:43,432 --> 00:06:45,432
- Woah, who's that new guy?
- Underoos!

86
00:06:45,442 --> 00:06:47,442
That's me! I gotta
go, I gotta go!

87
00:06:49,512 --> 00:06:51,512
Hey, everyone.

88
00:06:52,792 --> 00:06:55,832
Okay, so the craziest thing just happened, right?
I just had a fight with Captain America,

89
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:57,952
and I stole his shield and I threw it at him,
and I... What the hell...

90
00:06:57,952 --> 00:07:00,912
He's big now! I gotta go.
Hold on.

91
00:07:03,792 --> 00:07:07,132
It was, the most amazing thing that's ever
happened. So Mr. Stark's, "Hey, Underoos!"

92
00:07:07,132 --> 00:07:09,192
And I just sort of flipped in,
and I stole Cap's shield,

93
00:07:09,392 --> 00:07:11,392
and I was like,
"Hey, what's up, everybody?"

94
00:07:11,892 --> 00:07:14,072
Hey, just a second. Coming.

95
00:07:15,992 --> 00:07:19,632
- Hey!
- We have thin walls here.

96
00:07:20,952 --> 00:07:23,952
- What are you doing, a video diary?
- Yeah.

97
00:07:24,632 --> 00:07:28,272
- It's alright.
- I told him not to do it. He was filming everything.

98
00:07:29,872 --> 00:07:30,772
Hey, hey, hey...

99
00:07:30,792 --> 00:07:33,772
You know what, we should make
an alibi video for your aunt, anyway.

100
00:07:33,772 --> 00:07:34,852
You ready?

101
00:07:35,352 --> 00:07:37,842
Okay. Get in the frame.

102
00:07:37,842 --> 00:07:40,832
Hey, May. How are you doing? What are
you wearing? Something skimpy, I hope.

103
00:07:41,392 --> 00:07:44,608
Peter, that's inappropriate.
Let's start over. We can edit it.

104
00:07:44,632 --> 00:07:47,912
3, 1. Hey, May! My gosh...

105
00:07:48,812 --> 00:07:51,552
Wanted to tell you what an
incredible job...

106
00:07:51,732 --> 00:07:55,992
... your nephew did this weekend at the
Stark Internship retreat.

107
00:07:56,452 --> 00:07:59,528
- Everyone was impressed.
- Come on!

108
00:07:59,552 --> 00:08:02,312
- It's a friggin' merge, I'm sorry.
- This, 'cause you're not on Queens Boulevard.

109
00:08:02,312 --> 00:08:05,522
See, Happy is hoping to get
bumped up to Asset Management.

110
00:08:05,522 --> 00:08:08,272
He was forehead of security. And
before that, he was just a driver.

111
00:08:08,272 --> 00:08:10,272
That was a private conversation.

112
00:08:10,492 --> 00:08:13,092
I don't like joking about this. It was hard
for me to talk to you about that...

113
00:08:13,092 --> 00:08:16,562
- No seriously, was he snoring aboard the plane?
- Okay, here we go...

114
00:08:20,242 --> 00:08:22,332
- Happy, can you give us a moment?
- You want me to leave the car?

115
00:08:22,357 --> 00:08:24,859
I want you to grab Peter's
case out of the trunk.

116
00:08:25,484 --> 00:08:27,541
I can keep the suit?

117
00:08:27,566 --> 00:08:30,595
Yes, we were just talking about it.

118
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:33,018
Do me a favor, though...

119
00:08:33,042 --> 00:08:35,392
Happy's kinda your point guy in
this. Don't stress him out.

120
00:08:35,472 --> 00:08:38,032
Don't do anything stupid.
I've seen his cardiogram.

121
00:08:38,382 --> 00:08:40,428
- All right?
- Yes.

122
00:08:40,452 --> 00:08:43,472
Don't do anything I would do. And
definitely don't do anything I wouldn't do.

123
00:08:44,162 --> 00:08:47,352
There's a little gray area in there
and that's where you operate.

124
00:08:47,352 --> 00:08:49,352
- Wait, does that mean that I'm an Avenger?
- No.

125
00:08:49,892 --> 00:08:51,912
- He's at?
- Seventh floor.

126
00:08:51,912 --> 00:08:54,716
- I can take that up. You don't have to take it.
- You're gonna take it?

127
00:08:54,741 --> 00:08:57,112
- Yeah. I can take that.
- Thank you.

128
00:08:57,922 --> 00:09:02,292
- So, when's our next, "retreat", you know?
- What? Next mission?

129
00:09:02,292 --> 00:09:04,312
- Yeah, the mission, the mission.
- We'll call you.

130
00:09:04,552 --> 00:09:07,232
- Well did you have my number?
- No, I mean we'll call you.

131
00:09:07,432 --> 00:09:10,432
Like, someone will
call you. Alright?

132
00:09:11,372 --> 00:09:13,372
That's not a hug, I'm just
grabbing the door for you.

133
00:09:13,512 --> 00:09:15,512
We're not... we're not there yet.

134
00:09:17,622 --> 00:09:19,622
Bye!

135
00:09:23,712 --> 00:09:25,712
They're gonna call me.

136
00:09:29,872 --> 00:09:32,272
<font color="#ffff00">2 MONTHS LATER</font>

137
00:09:40,214 --> 00:09:42,614
<font color="#0080ff">Hey, Happy. Just write for fun.
i'm finished school on 14:45.</font>

138
00:09:42,615 --> 00:09:44,340
<font color="#0080ff">Ready for next mission!</font>

139
00:09:44,397 --> 00:09:45,841
<font color="#0080ff">This Peter, BTW.</font>

140
00:09:45,842 --> 00:09:46,842
<font color="#0080ff">Parker</font>

