- Thanks, Jason, but I already have a date.

146
00:10:26,312 --> 00:10:28,312
- Okay.
- Yep.

147
00:10:35,392 --> 00:10:36,992
You in my office, freak!

148
00:10:55,822 --> 00:11:00,032
Join me, and together, we'll
build my new Lego Death Star.

149
00:11:00,132 --> 00:11:01,932
- What?!
- So lame.

150
00:11:02,552 --> 00:11:04,432
No way, that's awesome!
How many pieces?

151
00:11:04,432 --> 00:11:05,832
3,803.

152
00:11:05,842 --> 00:11:07,848
- That's insane.
- I know!

153
00:11:07,872 --> 00:11:11,252
- You wanna build it tonight?
- I can't tonight. I got the Stark internship.

154
00:11:11,272 --> 00:11:12,968
- Stark internship.
- Yeah, exactly.

155
00:11:12,992 --> 00:11:16,112
- Boy's got that internship.
- Hopefully, soon it'll lead to a real job.

156
00:11:17,312 --> 00:11:19,832
That would be so sweet. He'd be all,

157
00:11:19,832 --> 00:11:21,832
"Good job on those spreadsheets,
Peter. Here's a gold coin."

158
00:11:23,022 --> 00:11:26,302
- I don't know how jobs work.
- That's exactly how they work.

159
00:11:26,822 --> 00:11:30,852
I'll knock out the basic bones of the Death Star
at my place, and then I'll come by afterwards.

160
00:11:30,852 --> 00:11:33,512
Because for the most part, 
the difficult thing will be just the base of it.

161
00:11:33,512 --> 00:11:36,152
The top half will....

162
00:11:37,772 --> 00:11:39,772
That'd be great.

163
00:11:40,112 --> 00:11:44,352
Okay, so how do we calculate linear
acceleration between points A and B?

164
00:11:46,192 --> 00:11:47,272
Flash.

165
00:11:47,272 --> 00:11:49,772
It's the product of sine of the
angle and gravity, divided by the mass.

166
00:11:49,772 --> 00:11:51,978
Nope. Peter.

167
00:11:52,402 --> 00:11:54,008
Are you still with us?

168
00:11:54,432 --> 00:11:57,192
Uh, yeah. Yeah. Uhh...

169
00:11:58,022 --> 00:12:00,592
Mass cancels out,
so it's just gravity times sine.

170
00:12:00,652 --> 00:12:02,742
Right. See, Flash?
Being the fastest...

171
00:12:02,767 --> 00:12:04,776
...isn't always the best
if you are wrong.

172
00:12:04,872 --> 00:12:06,272
You're dead.

173
00:12:10,152 --> 00:12:13,768
Today we're gonna be talking
about Danish physicist Neils Bohr.

174
00:12:13,792 --> 00:12:19,832
But trust me, there's nothing "Bohr-ing" about
his discoveries regarding quantum theory.

175
00:12:29,152 --> 00:12:31,152
Did Liz get a new top?

176
00:12:31,172 --> 00:12:33,712
No. We've seen that before, but...

177
00:12:33,712 --> 00:12:35,512
- ...never with that skirt.
- Liz!

178
00:12:35,512 --> 00:12:37,528
Hey!
That looks so good.

179
00:12:37,552 --> 00:12:40,312
We should probably stop staring
before it gets creepy, though.

180
00:12:40,322 --> 00:12:43,162
Too late. You guys are losers.

181
00:12:43,472 --> 00:12:46,822
- Then why do you sit with us?
- Because I don't have any friends.

182
00:12:49,012 --> 00:12:53,812
Let's move to the next question...
What is the heaviest naturally occuring element?

183
00:12:54,412 --> 00:12:57,982
Hydrogen's the lightest.
That's not the question. Ok.

184
00:12:58,132 --> 00:13:01,392
- Uranium.
- That is correct. Thank you, Abraham.

185
00:13:01,472 --> 00:13:03,548
Please open your books to page 10.

186
00:13:03,572 --> 00:13:05,572
Peter, it's nationals.

187
00:13:05,662 --> 00:13:08,606
Is there no way you could take
one weekend off?

188
00:13:08,692 --> 00:13:11,532
I can't go to Washington
because if Mr. Stark needs me,

189
00:13:11,532 --> 00:13:15,772
- then I have to make sure I'm here.
- You've never even been in the same room as Tony Stark.

190
00:13:15,772 --> 00:13:18,791
- Wait, what's happening?
- Peter's not going to Washington.

191
00:13:18,816 --> 00:13:21,978
- No, no, no, no, no.
- Why not?

192
00:13:22,602 --> 00:13:24,628
Really?
Right before nationals?

193
00:13:24,652 --> 00:13:26,772
You already quit marching
band and robotics lab.

194
00:13:28,652 --> 00:13:30,892
I'm not obsessed with him.
I'm just very observant.

195
00:13:31,462 --> 00:13:33,512
Flash, you're in for Peter.

196
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:36,052
Ooh.. I don't know. I gotta
check my calendar first.

197
00:13:36,082 --> 00:13:40,072
- I got a hot date with Black Widow coming up.
- That is false.

198
00:13:40,272 --> 00:13:42,842
What did I tell you about using the bell
for comedic purposes?

199
00:13:47,362 --> 00:13:55,806
<font color="#0080ff">[ SRT by imot ]</font>

200
00:14:01,132 --> 00:14:03,132
- Hey, what's up?
- Hey, man.

201
00:14:05,652 --> 00:14:08,312
- What's up, Mr. Delmar?
- Hey, Mr. Parker.

202
00:14:09,012 --> 00:14:10,268
Number five, right?

203
00:14:10,292 --> 00:14:13,372
Yeah, and with pickles. And can
you squish it down real flat?

204
00:14:13,372 --> 00:14:15,588
- Thanks.
- You got it, boss.

205
00:14:16,012 --> 00:14:19,468
- How's your aunt?
- Yeah, she's all right.

206
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:22,600
<font color="#ffff00"><i>"La bella donna italiana bellissima"</i></font>
His aunt is a beautiful Italian woman.

207
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:25,900
<font color="#ffff00"><i>"Como estas tua figlia?"</i></font>
How's your daughter?

208
00:14:27,642 --> 00:14:30,282
- You know what? $10.
- It's $5!

209
00:14:30,782 --> 00:14:33,962
- For that comment, $10.
- Hey. Come on, I'm joking. I'm joking.

210
00:14:35,412 --> 00:14:37,412
Here's $5.

211
00:14:38,572 --> 00:14:40,572
What's up, Murph?

212
00:14:40,852 --> 00:14:42,852
How you doing, buddy?

213
00:14:45,252 --> 00:14:48,578
- How's school?
- You know. It's boring. I got better things to do.

214
00:14:49,002 --> 00:14:52,552
Stay in school, kids. Stay in school.
Otherwise, you're gonna end up like me.

215
00:14:53,132 --> 00:14:56,362
- This is great.
- Best sandwiches in Queens.

216
00:16:17,472 --> 00:16:20,922
Hey, could you hold
this for a second? Thanks.

217
00:16:21,532 --> 00:16:24,348
Hey, is this anybody's bike? No?

218
00:16:25,372 --> 00:16:27,948
- Hey, buddy, is this your bike?
- No change.

219
00:16:27,972 --> 00:16:30,052
Does anyone have a pen,
do you have a pen?

220
00:16:30,115 --> 00:16:32,715
<font color="#ffff00">IS THIS YOUR BIKE?
IF NOT, DON'T STEAL IT!
*SPIDER-MAN</font>

