00:32:26,052 --> 00:32:31,952
- I got, black hole grenades, Chitauri rail guns...
- ... Letting off shots in public.

456
00:32:32,032 --> 00:32:34,232
No, I hear you.
Look, times are changing,

457
00:32:34,312 --> 00:32:38,112
and we're the only ones selling
these high tech weapons.

458
00:32:38,132 --> 00:32:40,432
This must be where the ATM
robbers got their stuff.

459
00:32:40,452 --> 00:32:44,818
I just need something to stakeout somebody.
I'm not trying to shoot them back in time.

460
00:32:44,842 --> 00:32:48,192
- I got anti-grav climbers...
- You have climbers?

461
00:32:50,472 --> 00:32:52,472
Okay, what the hell was that?

462
00:32:54,512 --> 00:32:56,512
- Did you set us up?
- Hey, hey, man!

463
00:32:59,032 --> 00:33:01,622
Hey, hey. C'mon! You're gonna
shoot at somebody, shoot at me!

464
00:33:02,162 --> 00:33:04,162
All right.

465
00:33:15,432 --> 00:33:17,432
What was that?

466
00:33:28,472 --> 00:33:31,392
- We gotta call him.
- Nah, nah, nah, nah!

467
00:33:36,912 --> 00:33:39,678
- Did you just do it again?
- Shut up!

468
00:33:39,702 --> 00:33:41,702
I'm calling him.

469
00:33:47,762 --> 00:33:50,266
Toomes' phone.

470
00:33:50,591 --> 00:33:52,228
Boss...

471
00:33:52,252 --> 00:33:54,252
Oww. My butt.

472
00:34:12,492 --> 00:34:15,252
Great. Guess I'm gonna
have to take a shortcut.

473
00:34:17,222 --> 00:34:19,222
Hey, guys. Good game. Have fun.

474
00:34:19,812 --> 00:34:23,692
Hey! Buddy! Sorry, no time
to play. Here. Go fetch!

475
00:34:25,932 --> 00:34:27,932
Now this is more like it!

476
00:34:39,852 --> 00:34:41,852
Smells really good!

477
00:34:44,732 --> 00:34:46,732
Great movie!

478
00:34:51,892 --> 00:34:53,892
Oh, hey girls.

479
00:34:56,862 --> 00:35:00,568
- Hey, it's Peter. Leave a message.
- Peter, where are you?

480
00:35:00,592 --> 00:35:02,892
That's not working. This is not cool.

481
00:35:03,782 --> 00:35:05,782
Almost got you!

482
00:35:17,292 --> 00:35:19,292
Thought you'd get away
from me, didn't you?

483
00:35:20,372 --> 00:35:22,372
I gotcha! Right
where I want you!

484
00:35:22,612 --> 00:35:24,612
Surprise!

485
00:35:28,012 --> 00:35:29,612
What the hell?

486
00:36:14,372 --> 00:36:16,372
Oh. Hey.

487
00:36:19,712 --> 00:36:22,512
And then, he's, he just, like swooped down,
like a monster. And

488
00:36:22,602 --> 00:36:26,542
He picked me up and took me over like 1000
feet and just dropped me.

489
00:36:26,652 --> 00:36:29,082
How did you find me? Did you put
a tracker on my suit or something?

490
00:36:29,882 --> 00:36:31,882
I put everything in your suit.

491
00:36:32,492 --> 00:36:34,492
Including this heater.

492
00:36:37,332 --> 00:36:41,108
- That's better. Thanks.
- What were you thinking?

493
00:36:41,332 --> 00:36:44,752
The guy with the wings is obviously the
source of the weapons. I gotta take him down.

494
00:36:45,022 --> 00:36:47,048
Take him down now, huh?

495
00:36:47,072 --> 00:36:50,852
- Steady, Crockett. There are people who handle this sort of thing.
- The Avengers?

496
00:36:51,252 --> 00:36:53,202
No, no, no. This is a little
below their paygrade.

497
00:36:53,202 --> 00:36:57,052
Anyway, Mr. Stark. You didn't have to come
all the way out here. I had that. I was fine.

498
00:36:57,692 --> 00:37:00,212
Oh, I'm not... here.

499
00:37:01,552 --> 00:37:05,332
Thank God, this place has Wi-Fi,
or you would be toast right now.

500
00:37:05,432 --> 00:37:07,432
Thank Ganesh while you're at it.

501
00:37:09,252 --> 00:37:12,218
- Look, forget the flying Vulture guy. Please!
- Why?

502
00:37:12,243 --> 00:37:14,812
Why? Because I said so!

503
00:37:15,272 --> 00:37:17,412
Sorry. I'm talking to a teenager.

504
00:37:18,232 --> 00:37:22,052
Stay close to the ground. Build up your
game, helping the little people.

505
00:37:22,522 --> 00:37:24,612
Like that lady that
bought you the churro.

506
00:37:25,122 --> 00:37:29,892
Can't you just be like a friendly,
neighborhood Spider-Man?

507
00:37:29,912 --> 00:37:31,912
But I'm ready for
more than that now.

508
00:37:32,732 --> 00:37:34,402
No, you're not.

509
00:37:34,402 --> 00:37:36,592
That is not what you thought
when I took on Captain America.

510
00:37:36,682 --> 00:37:39,692
Trust me, kid. If Cap wanted
to lay you out, he would have.

511
00:37:39,892 --> 00:37:43,772
Listen to me. If you come across
these weapons again, call Happy.

512
00:37:44,812 --> 00:37:46,212
Are you driving?

513
00:37:46,542 --> 00:37:48,932
You know, it's never too early
to start thinking about college.

514
00:37:49,412 --> 00:37:51,732
I got some pull at MIT. End call.

515
00:37:53,052 --> 00:37:56,372
- No, I don't need to go to college, Mr. Stark...
- Mr. Stark is no longer connected.

516
00:37:59,792 --> 00:38:01,792
That's awesome.

517
00:38:04,212 --> 00:38:07,132
Stay close to the ground.
What is he talking about?

518
00:38:28,162 --> 00:38:33,202
- Hey, man, what's up? I'm on my way back.
- Actually, I was calling to say maybe you shouldn't come. Listen to this.

519
00:38:33,252 --> 00:38:35,772
... When I say "Penis",
you say "Parker"!

520
00:38:38,982 --> 00:38:42,452
Sorry, Peter. I guess we're still
losers. I'll see you tomorrow.

521
00:38:42,492 --> 00:38:44,492
I'll see you tomorrow in school.

522
00:39:26,892 --> 00:39:28,892
Idiots.

523
00:39:29,492 --> 00:39:32,417
Idiots. Idiots!

524
00:39:33,642 --> 00:39:35,068
Boss?

525
00:39:35,092 --> 00:39:38,772
Your wife keeps texting you.
Something about a brake light?

526
00:39:38,892 --> 00:39:40,978
What'd I tell you about
looking at my phone?

527
00:39:41,002 --> 00:39:44,812
Oh, sorry. You left it out. You
know I'm a curious person by nature.

528
00:39:47,012 --> 00:39:50,002
I've finished designing that
high altitude vacuum seal...

529
00:39:51,202 --> 00:39:54,732
In case you wanna, you
know, go for the big one?

530
00:39:54,822 --> 00:39:58,932
You're still on that? I told you,
no. The answer's no. Forget it!

531
00:40:11,612 --> 00:40:13,612
That was badass.

532
00:40:16,302 --> 00:40:20,192
How many times have I told you...
Not to fire them out in the open?

533
00:40:20,192 --> 00:40:24,072
- You said move the merchandise!
- Under the radar. Under the radar!

534
00:40:24,722 --> 00:40:26,722
That's how we survive.

535
00:40:26,932 --> 00:40:30,362
If you bring Damage Control, or
the Avengers down here, we're through.

536
00:40:30,762 --> 00:40:34,002
And you're out there, wearing
that goofy thing, lighting up cars...

537
00:40:34,062 --> 00:40:37,772
Calling yourself "The Shocker."
I'm the Shocker. I shock people.

538
00:40:37,852 --> 00:40:41,002
- What is this, pro wrestling?
- Yeah, whatever, old man. C'mon.

539
00:40:43,002 --> 00:40:45,172
Look, look.

540
00:40:46,352 --> 00:40:50,412
I know, you don't give a
crap about anything. But I do.

541
00:40:51,232 --> 00:40:54,142
I built this whole place because
I got people I have to look after.

542
00:40:54,162 --> 00:40:56,532
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

543
00:41:00,512 --> 00:41:04,292
You know what? I can't
afford your bullshit.

544
00:41:05,232 --> 00:41:06,838
- Get outta here.
- What?!

545
00:41:06,862 --> 00:41:10,212
- You're done, you're off the crew.
- Yeah. Alright.

546
00:41:12,532 --> 00:41:14,812
Wonder if you can
afford me out there...

547
00:41:14,972 --> 00:41:19,122
- With everything I know.
- Excuse me?

548
00:41:19,142 --> 00:41:21,168
I'm just saying...

549
00:41:21,592 --> 00:41:24,632
Maybe your wife would like to know
where you really get your money from.

550
00:41:26,292 --> 00:41:28,292
- You know what?
- What?

551
00:41:28,362 --> 00:41:29,648
You're right.

552
00:41:29,872 --> 00:41:31,872
- That work?
- I don't know.

553
00:41:32,802 --> 00:41:34,802
I can't afford that.

554
00:41:44,102 --> 00:41:46,102
Damn!

555
00:41:48,452 --> 00:41:50,772
- I thought this was the anti-gravity gun.
- What?!

556
00:41:51,122 --> 00:41:54,122
No. That's that one.

557
00:42:06,342 --> 00:42:08,342
Here.

558
00:42:08,372 --> 00:42:12,172
Now you're the Shocker. Go out there
and find that weapon he lost.

559
00:42:12,732 --> 00:42:14,532
Right.

560
00:42:23,992 --> 00:42:27,792
- Hey, thanks for bailing on me.
- Yeah, well, something came up.

561
00:42:27,822 --> 00:42:30,712
- What is that?
- I don't know.

562
00:42:30,712 --> 00:42:33,592
- Some guy tried to vaporize me with it.
- Seriously?

563
00:42:33,617 --> 00:42:35,628
- Yeah.
- Awesome!

564
00:42:35,652 --> 00:42:37,652
I mean, not awesome.

565
00:42:37,732 --> 00:42:40,132
Totally uncool, that guy. So scary.

566
00:42:42,852 --> 00:42:46,332
Well look. I think it's a power source.

567
00:42:46,732 --> 00:42:49,462
Yeah, but it's connected
to all those microprocessors.

568
00:42:49,462 --> 00:42:52,492
It's an inductive charging plate.
That's what I use to charge my toothbrush.

569
00:42:52,792 --> 00:42:55,802
Whoever's making these weapons is
obviously combining the alien tech with ours.

570
00:42:56,012 --> 00:43:00,082
That is literally the coolest
sentence anyone has ever said.

571
00:43:00,092 --> 00:43:05,072
I just wanna thank you for letting me be
a part of your journey, into this amazing...

572
00:43:09,142 --> 00:43:12,172
Keep your fingers
clear of the blades.

573
00:43:14,952 --> 00:43:16,962
I gotta figure out what
this thing is and who makes it.

574
00:43:17,022 --> 00:43:19,332
We'll go to the lab after
class and run some tests.

575
00:43:28,572 --> 00:43:31,372
First, I say we put
the glowy thing in the mass spectrometer.

576
00:43:31,652 --> 00:43:34,012
First, we gotta come up with
a better name than "glowy thingy".

577
00:43:34,212 --> 00:43:35,712
You're right.

578
00:43:36,832 --> 00:43:40,652
Crap!
Come on, come on, come on.

579
00:43:45,522 --> 00:43:47,522
High schools creep me out.

580
00:43:48,052 --> 00:43:50,052
It's got this funny smell,
you know what I mean?

581
00:43:50,182 --> 00:43:53,678
- That's one of the guys that tried to kill me.
- What?

582
00:43:53,702 --> 00:43:57,652
- We gotta get out of here.
- No, no, no. We got to follow them.

583
00:43:57,652 --> 00:43:59,992
Maybe they can lead me to the
guy that dropped me in a lake.

584
00:44:00,172 --> 00:44:02,292
- Someone dropped you in a lake?
- Yeah. It was not good.

585
00:44:03,752 --> 00:44:05,788
- Peter.
- No. Stay there, Ned.

586
00:44:06,412 --> 00:44:08,112
Peter!

587
00:44:11,212 --> 00:44:14,068
- What are you doing?
- Nothing.

588
00:44:14,092 --> 00:44:16,092
Yeah. You good?

589
00:44:16,812 --> 00:44:18,812
Chess?

590
00:44:20,652 --> 00:44:23,692
Can you imagine what the boss
would say if he knew where we were?

591
00:44:24,332 --> 00:44:26,712
I'm saying there was
an energy pulse right here.

592
00:44:26,752 --> 00:44:30,422
There's no sign of the weapon. I
mean, even if it was here, now it's gone.

593
00:44:30,492 --> 00:44:32,492
So are we...

594
00:45:02,182 --> 00:45:04,332
This is so awesome.

595
00:45:05,092 --> 00:45:07,092
I know, right.

596
00:45:10,012 --> 00:45:12,012
In Brooklyn.

597
00:45:15,442 --> 00:45:17,442
Staten Island.

598
00:45:22,692 --> 00:45:24,692
Leaving Jersey.

599
00:45:31,172 --> 00:45:32,472
They stopped.

600
00:45:35,372 --> 00:45:37,272
- Maryland?
- What's there?

601
00:45:37,292 --> 00:45:39,752
I don't know, evil lair?

602
00:45:40,032 --> 00:45:42,812
- Evil lair?
- Dude, a gang with alien guns run by a guy with wings,

603
00:45:42,812 --> 00:45:45,518
- yeah, they have a lair.
- Badass.

604
00:45:45,542 --> 00:45:48,292
But, how are you gonna get there
if that's like, 300 miles away?

605
00:45:49,792 --> 00:45:51,792
It's not too far from DC.

606
00:45:53,042 --> 00:45:55,252
- Hey, it's Peter!
- Guys!

607
00:45:55,252 --> 00:45:58,318
- Yeah, I was hoping maybe I could rejoin the team.
- No. No way.

608
00:45:58,342 --> 00:46:00,892
You can't just quit on us, stroll
up, and be welcomed back by everyone.

609
00:46:00,972 --> 00:46:04,128
Hey, welcome back, Peter! Flash,
you're back to first alternate.

610
00:46:04,152 --> 00:46:05,358
- What?
- He's taking your place!

611
00:46:05,382 --> 00:46:07,388
Excuse me, can we go already?

612
00:46:07,412 --> 00:46:10,512
'Cause I was hoping to get in some light protesting in
front of one of the embassies before dinner, so...

613
00:46:10,542 --> 00:46:13,022
Protesting is patriotic.
Let's get on the bus.

614
00:46:14,772 --> 00:46:17,652
Focus up, everyone. Our next
topic is the moons of Saturn.

615
00:46:18,012 --> 00:46:21,108
- The second law of Thermodynamics.
- Frank Sinatra.

616
00:46:21,132 --> 00:46:23,412
- Fort Sumpter.
- Flash is wrong.

617
00:46:23,452 --> 00:46:25,792
- Okay guys, let's focus. Next one.
- Liz, don't overwork 'em.

618
00:46:26,452 --> 00:46:30,252
- Strontium, Barium, Vibranium.
- Very good, Peter. Glad to have you back.

619
00:46:30,252 --> 00:46:32,152
Glad to be back.

620
00:46:32,212 --> 00:46:34,268
What is the current state of unit...

621
00:46:34,292 --> 00:46:36,312
- Can I take this real quick? I'll only be a second.
- Yeah, fine.

622
00:46:36,402 --> 00:46:39,392
- Hello?
- I got a blip on my screen here. You left New York?

623
00:46:39,412 --> 00:46:41,308
Tracker. Uh, yeah...

624
00:46:41,332 --> 00:46:43,172
No, it's just a school trip,
it's nothing. Look, Happy...

625
00:46:43,372 --> 00:46:47,212
I gotta say, you tracking me without my
permission is a complete violation of my privacy.

626
00:46:47,522 --> 00:46:49,388
- That's different.
- What's different?

627
00:46:49,412 --> 00:46:51,292
Nothing. Look, it's
just the academic decathlon.

628
00:46:51,372 --> 00:46:54,242
- It's no big deal.
- Hey. I'll decide if it's no big deal.

629
00:46:56,512 --> 00:46:59,142
Sounds like it's no big deal.
But remember, I'm watching you.

630
00:47:08,972 --> 00:47:10,972
- Everyone stick together.
- Yeah.

631
00:47:11,972 --> 00:47:13,972
Are you kidding me?
This place is huge!

632
00:47:13,992 --> 00:47:15,952
- I've seen bigger.
- There's a bird in here.

633
00:47:16,012 --> 00:47:19,628
- Hey, you brought your laptop, right?
- Why?

634
00:47:26,572 --> 00:47:30,472
Peter, why are we removing
the tracker from your suit?

635
00:47:32,292 --> 00:47:35,332
Because I gotta follow these guys
to their boss before they move again...

636
00:47:35,502 --> 00:47:37,792
And I don't really want
Mr. Stark to know about it.

637
00:47:37,852 --> 00:47:41,458
- So you're lying to Iron Man now?
- No, I'm not lying.

638
00:47:41,482 --> 00:47:43,482
He just doesn't really
get what I can do yet.

639
00:47:47,772 --> 00:47:49,248
Gotcha.

640
00:47:49,272 --> 00:47:53,652
Alright, Happy. Enjoy tracking this lamp.

641
00:47:55,402 --> 00:47:58,052
There's a ton of
other subsystems in here.

642
00:47:59,012 --> 00:48:02,502
But they're all disabled by the...
"Training Wheels Protocol".

643
00:48:02,502 --> 00:48:05,572
What? The Training Wheels Protocol?

644
00:48:05,732 --> 00:48:08,172
- Turn it off.
- I don't think that's a good idea, I mean...

645
00:48:08,172 --> 00:48:10,228
They're probably
blocked for a reason.

646
00:48:10,252 --> 00:48:12,012
Come on, man. I don't
need training wheels.

647
00:48:12,092 --> 00:48:14,172
I'm sick of him treating me
like a kid all the time.

648
00:48:14,332 --> 00:48:16,478
- It's not cool.
- But you are a kid.

649
00:48:16,502 --> 00:48:18,732
Yeah. A kid who can stop
a bus with his bare hands.

650
00:48:18,812 --> 00:48:22,388
Peter, I just don't think this is a great
idea. I mean, what if this is illegal?

651
00:48:22,412 --> 00:48:25,252
Look, please. This is my
chance to prove myself.

652
00:48:25,562 --> 00:48:28,428
- I can handle it. Ned, come on.
- I really don't think this is a good idea.

653
00:48:28,452 --> 00:48:30,970
- But, guy in the chair.
- Don't do that!

654
00:48:30,995 --> 00:48:33,056
Come on.

655
00:48:44,742 --> 00:48:46,712
Hey. The glowy thing is evidence.
Keep it safe, all right?

656
00:48:46,732 --> 00:48:47,932
Okay.

657
00:48:49,372 --> 00:48:51,372
- I'm moving.
- Be careful.

658
00:48:54,392 --> 00:48:57,492
- Hey, Liz.
- Perfect timing. We're gonna go swimming.

659
00:48:57,532 --> 00:48:59,332
Come on! Come on.

660
00:48:59,452 --> 00:49:01,452
Hey, Peter.

661
00:49:04,732 --> 00:49:08,012
I was gonna go study,
in the, business center.

662
00:49:08,132 --> 00:49:10,172
Peter, you don't need to study.
You're like the smartest guy I've ever met.

663
00:49:10,212 --> 00:49:12,212
And besides...

664
00:49:12,242 --> 00:49:15,362
A rebellious group activity the day
before competition is good for morale.

665
00:49:16,482 --> 00:49:18,552
Um, I read that in a TED talk, so...

666
00:49:18,552 --> 00:49:20,352
I heard it in a TED talk.

667
00:49:20,402 --> 00:49:22,402
And I read a coaching book.

668
00:49:23,262 --> 00:49:25,162
Are you really, this
is really important to you?

669
00:49:25,312 --> 00:49:27,212
Yeah. It's our future.

670
00:49:27,272 --> 00:49:29,272
I'm not gonna screw it up.

671
00:49:29,422 --> 00:49:33,172
And besides, we raided the minibar
and these candy bars were like $11.

672
00:49:33,212 --> 00:49:35,652
So get your trunks
on and come on.

673
00:49:35,732 --> 00:49:39,332
- Come on. Come on.
- I'm coming!

674
00:50:01,112 --> 00:50:03,412
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Good evening, Peter.</i></font>
- Hello?

675
00:50:03,612 --> 00:50:06,612
<font color="#ff8040">Congratulations on completing
your rigorous Training Wheels Protocol.</font>

676
00:50:06,672 --> 00:50:09,292
<font color="#ff8040"><i>And gaining access to your suit's
full capabilities.</i></font>

677
00:50:09,292 --> 00:50:12,252
- Ah, thank you.
<font color="#ff8040">- So where would you like to take me tonight?</font>

678
00:50:12,252 --> 00:50:15,352
I put a tracker on someone.
He's a bad guy.

679
00:50:15,422 --> 00:50:17,422
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Tracker located.</i></font>

680
00:50:18,212 --> 00:50:20,332
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Plotting course to intercept target.</i></font>

681
00:50:20,412 --> 00:50:23,492
Okay well, as long as I make it
back in time for decathlon, it's fine.

682
00:50:31,442 --> 00:50:33,812
<i><font color="#ff8040">100 meters from destination and closing.</font></i>

683
00:50:34,132 --> 00:50:36,132
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Jump now.</i></font>

684
00:50:40,142 --> 00:50:42,232
<i><font color="#ff8040">Detecting three individuals.</font></i>

685
00:50:43,282 --> 00:50:46,652
Why is their secret lair in
a gas station? That's so lame.

686
00:50:50,252 --> 00:50:53,712
- Hey, suit lady, what are they doing?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Do you wanna hear what they're saying?</i></font>

687
00:50:53,712 --> 00:50:56,172
I can hear what they're saying?
Uhh, yeah.

688
00:50:56,172 --> 00:50:58,172
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Activating Enhanced Reconnaissance mode.</i></font>

689
00:50:58,252 --> 00:51:00,812
I got the gauntlet from the Lagos cleanup.
The rest is all mine.

690
00:51:00,892 --> 00:51:02,948
Whoa. That's so cool.

691
00:51:02,972 --> 00:51:05,212
Can't believe they're still
cleaning up that Triskelion mess.

692
00:51:05,232 --> 00:51:08,472
I love it. They keep making
messes, we keep getting rich.

693
00:51:08,712 --> 00:51:11,538
- Target inbound.
- Whoa, they're in the middle of a heist.

694
00:51:11,562 --> 00:51:14,532
I can catch them all
red-handed. This is awesome!

695
00:51:15,012 --> 00:51:17,132
Okay, I'm gonna get a little closer
so I can see what's happening.

696
00:51:17,722 --> 00:51:20,552
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Would you like me to engage
Enhanced Combat mode?</i></font>

697
00:51:20,652 --> 00:51:23,052
"Enhanced Combat mode"? Yeah.

698
00:51:23,172 --> 00:51:27,362
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Activating Instant Kill.</i></font>
- No, no, no, no. I don't wanna kill anybody.

699
00:51:27,662 --> 00:51:29,662
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Deactivating Instant Kill.</i></font>

700
00:51:33,362 --> 00:51:35,362
Did you hear that?

701
00:51:35,772 --> 00:51:37,892
What the hell just happened?
What was that?

702
00:51:38,012 --> 00:51:40,641
<i><font color="#ff8040">You jumped off the sign and landed
on your face.</font></i>

703
00:51:43,466 --> 00:51:45,308
Suit lady, what's wrong
with my web shooters?

704
00:51:45,432 --> 00:51:48,012
<i><font color="#ff8040">Rapid-fire is the default
for Enhanced Combat mode.</font></i>

705
00:51:48,012 --> 00:51:50,998
- Why would I need Rapid-fire?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Would you like to see more options?</i></font>

706
00:51:51,022 --> 00:51:54,332
<font color="#ff8040"><i>You have 576 possible
web shooter combinations.</i></font>

707
00:51:54,882 --> 00:51:57,812
- Mr. Stark really overdid it.
- You two wait right here.

708
00:51:58,812 --> 00:52:02,532
Wait, you're gonna wanna turn on the dampers
or that thing will shatter your arm.

709
00:52:03,292 --> 00:52:05,428
- Where's the dampers?
- That one!

710
00:52:05,453 --> 00:52:08,932
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Great choice! Would you like me
to set this as your new default?</i></font>

711
00:52:10,462 --> 00:52:12,705
- No, no, no!
- Push that in...

712
00:52:12,730 --> 00:52:14,748
- Right here?
- No, no. Yeah, push it.

713
00:52:15,572 --> 00:52:17,812
- What was that?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Taser webs.</i></font>

714
00:52:17,932 --> 00:52:19,988
Taser webs? I don't
want taser webs.

715
00:52:20,012 --> 00:52:22,772
<font color="#ff8040"><i>You seem to be very unfamiliar
with your web shooter settings.</i></font>

716
00:52:23,652 --> 00:52:26,872
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Would you like to run a refresher course?</i></font>
- No, just, you choose.

717
00:52:26,932 --> 00:52:28,032
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Sure thing.</i></font>

718
00:52:28,324 --> 00:52:30,924
<i>6-Alpha-9er, are you running on time?</i>

719
00:52:31,492 --> 00:52:35,132
<i>Copy, Central. 6-Alpha-9er, on schedule.</i>

720
00:52:39,092 --> 00:52:41,092
- I have a visual.
- Green light. Green light.

721
00:52:46,612 --> 00:52:48,612
That's him.

722
00:52:52,292 --> 00:52:54,372
Okay. I got eyes on the convoy.

723
00:52:54,532 --> 00:52:56,532
Pulling in behind the cabooze.

724
00:52:57,812 --> 00:52:59,812
Deploy anchors.

725
00:53:11,052 --> 00:53:13,052
Dropping down.

726
00:53:15,502 --> 00:53:17,932
No outgoing distress signals.
You're all clear.

727
00:53:20,572 --> 00:53:22,572
Looks like they got
some good stuff here.

728
00:53:33,032 --> 00:53:35,652
Cool. It's like some kind
of matter phase shifter.

729
00:53:41,212 --> 00:53:43,212
All right. Coming up.

730
00:53:49,272 --> 00:53:51,772
Hey, big bird! This
doesn't belong to you!

731
00:53:52,732 --> 00:53:54,732
Oh, God.

732
00:54:01,932 --> 00:54:04,092
- Suit lady, what was that?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- You told me to choose.</i></font>

733
00:54:06,152 --> 00:54:08,972
What, no. Just set
everything back to normal!

734
00:54:09,292 --> 00:54:11,332
Activating all systems.

735
00:54:30,762 --> 00:54:34,332
- Oh. My head.
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- You appear to have a mild concussion.</i></font>

736
00:54:40,352 --> 00:54:44,068
- Hey, where am I right now?
- I'm not sure.

737
00:54:44,492 --> 00:54:46,852
<font color="#ff8040"><i>The container walls
are hindering my sensors.</i></font>

738
00:54:48,012 --> 00:54:50,028
Wait a minute.

739
00:54:50,052 --> 00:54:52,772
They must've hijacked the truck
and taken me to their evil lair.

740
00:54:54,552 --> 00:54:57,292
Okay suit lady. Maybe we're gonna have
to fight our way out of this one.

741
00:54:57,412 --> 00:54:59,412
Three, two, one!

742
00:55:06,512 --> 00:55:09,882
What is this place?
Suit lady, where am I?

743
00:55:09,882 --> 00:55:12,732
<font color="#ff8040"><i>You're in the most secure
facility on the eastern seaboard.</i></font>

744
00:55:13,362 --> 00:55:15,388
<font color="#ff8040"><i>The Damage Control
deep storage vault.</i></font>

745
00:55:15,412 --> 00:55:17,412
No! Seriously?

746
00:55:21,332 --> 00:55:23,972
<font color="#ff8040"><i>The door will most likely
remain closed until morning.</i></font>

747
00:55:24,752 --> 00:55:26,828
Morning?

748
00:55:26,852 --> 00:55:31,492
Hey, suit lady. I kinda feel bad
calling you "Suit Lady", you know?

749
00:55:32,252 --> 00:55:35,348
I think I should
probably give you a name.

750
00:55:35,372 --> 00:55:38,692
The Liz. No, no,
no. God, that's weird.

751
00:55:40,172 --> 00:55:45,218
- What about Karen?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- You can call me Karen if you'd like.</i></font>

752
00:55:45,442 --> 00:55:47,772
Hey, Karen. What else
can this suit do?

753
00:55:49,452 --> 00:55:52,852
What? Maybe we should run
that refresher course.

754
00:55:53,772 --> 00:55:55,772
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Ricochet web.</i></font>
- Ricochet web.

755
00:55:56,732 --> 00:55:57,622
Cool.

756
00:55:57,705 --> 00:55:59,105
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Splitter Web.</i></font>

757
00:56:00,932 --> 00:56:03,972
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Web grenade.</i></font>
- Web grenade!

758
00:56:05,852 --> 00:56:08,092
Should I tell Liz
that I'm Spider-Man?

759
00:56:09,412 --> 00:56:13,252
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Who's Liz?</i></font>
- Who's Liz?

760
00:56:13,892 --> 00:56:17,732
She's the best. She's awesome.
She's just a girl who goes to my school.

761
00:56:19,452 --> 00:56:24,312
And, yeah. I really wanna tell her,
but it's kinda weird. You know?

762
00:56:24,842 --> 00:56:29,628
- "Hey. I'm Spider-Man."
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- What's weird about that?</i></font>

763
00:56:29,652 --> 00:56:34,912
What if she's expecting someone like Tony Stark?
Imagine how disappointed she'd be when she sees me.

764
00:56:35,132 --> 00:56:38,868
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Well, if I were her,
I wouldn't be disappointed at all.</i></font>

765
00:56:39,292 --> 00:56:42,932
Thanks, Karen.
It's really nice to have somebody to talk to.

766
00:56:44,372 --> 00:56:47,138
- Hey, how long have we been here, anyway?
<i><font color="#ff8040">- 37 minutes.</font></i>

767
00:56:47,363 --> 00:56:50,508
What? 37 minutes? That's insane!

768
00:56:50,532 --> 00:56:54,482
I cannot take this anymore.
I gotta get out of here.

769
00:56:56,052 --> 00:56:58,492
There's gotta be something
in here I can use.

770
00:57:00,092 --> 00:57:02,092
Okay, let's see.

771
00:57:03,052 --> 00:57:05,052
Nope.

772
00:57:06,252 --> 00:57:10,732
That's awesome. Hey, it's
like the glowy thing.

773
00:57:11,332 --> 00:57:13,952
<font color="#ff8040"><i>That glowy thing is an
explosive Chitauri energy core.</i></font>

774
00:57:14,852 --> 00:57:20,532
- Whoa, you mean we've been carrying around a bomb?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- It would require radiation to transform it into an explosive state.</i></font>

775
00:57:22,302 --> 00:57:24,302
No, no, no, no!

776
00:57:28,592 --> 00:57:32,012
Hey, please! Please!
Somebody let me out! Hey!

777
00:57:32,132 --> 00:57:34,212
Karen you have to help me
override that timelock!

778
00:57:34,772 --> 00:57:38,248
- Okay, Karen, lower the voltage and run it.
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Trial unsuccessful.</i></font>

779
00:57:38,272 --> 00:57:40,272
Okay, we're just gonna
have to try every sequence.

780
00:57:44,692 --> 00:57:47,292
Ned, Peter, we're gonna
be late. Come on. Let's go.

781
00:57:48,492 --> 00:57:50,492
Okay. Hold on, hold on.

782
00:57:55,262 --> 00:57:57,892
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Initiating trial 247.</i></font>

783
00:57:59,052 --> 00:58:01,052
It worked! It works!

784
00:58:13,942 --> 00:58:17,772
<i>Please be sure all
cellphones are turned off.</i>

785
00:58:18,612 --> 00:58:21,006
Karen, you have to get me to the
decathlon as fast as possible!

786
00:58:21,031 --> 00:58:24,078
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Sure thing. Just tell me where it is.</i></font>
- It's right across the street from the Washington Monument.

787
00:58:24,102 --> 00:58:27,172
- Hey, it's Ned. Leave a message.
- Ned, call me back! The glowy thing's a bomb!

788
00:58:32,052 --> 00:58:34,052
<font color="#ff8040"><i>There's a vehicle
approaching on your right.</i></font>

789
00:58:34,452 --> 00:58:36,552
<i>We have now entered
sudden death.</i>

790
00:58:36,572 --> 00:58:39,812
<i>The next correct answer
wins the championship.</i>

791
00:58:43,932 --> 00:58:47,988
<i>- Midtown Tech?
- Zero.</i>

792
00:58:48,012 --> 00:58:51,532
<i>That is correct. Midtown
takes the championship!</i>

793
00:58:53,212 --> 00:58:55,212
- We won!
- Guys, I'm so proud of you!

794
00:58:55,251 --> 00:58:56,268
Told you we don't need Peter.

795
00:58:56,492 --> 00:58:58,412
Flash, you didn't answer
a single question.

796
00:58:58,502 --> 00:58:59,988
Taking it all in, Michelle?

797
00:59:00,012 --> 00:59:04,172
Oh, yeah, I just umm, I don't really wanna
celebrate something that was built by slaves.

798
00:59:04,212 --> 00:59:06,762
Oh, I'm sure the Washington
Monument wasn't built by...

799
00:59:09,952 --> 00:59:12,232
Okay. Enjoy your book.

800
00:59:12,557 --> 00:59:14,091
Thanks.

801
00:59:15,852 --> 00:59:18,292
- Oh, Ned. You're alive!
- Peter, are you okay?

802
00:59:18,432 --> 00:59:21,492
- Ned, Ned, where's the glowy thing?
- Don't worry. It's safe. It's in my backpack.

803
00:59:21,532 --> 00:59:23,583
No, Ned! Listen! No, Ned!
The glowy thing is dangerous!

804
00:59:23,608 --> 00:59:25,789
You missed the decathlon.
I covered for you...

805
00:59:25,814 --> 00:59:27,668
- Ned, listen to me!
- We're in the Washington Monument. How're you gonna...

806
00:59:27,693 --> 00:59:28,749
- Peter, is that you?
- Oh, hey, Liz!

807
00:59:28,774 --> 00:59:30,833
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Is that Liz?</i></font>
- Please put Ned back on the phone.

808
00:59:30,858 --> 00:59:33,758
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- You should tell her how you feel.</i></font>
- Seriously, you are so lucky we won!

809
00:59:33,782 --> 00:59:36,528
You know, I wanna be mad, but I'm real worried.
Like, what is going on with you?

810
00:59:37,252 --> 00:59:40,228
- Liz, I have to talk to Ned, it's really important!
- Miss, all items on the belt, please.

811
00:59:40,252 --> 00:59:42,772
Liz, there's something in his backpack
that is really dangerous. Don't let it go through an x-ray.

812
00:59:46,252 --> 00:59:48,252
Liz? Liz?
Dammit!

813
00:59:51,862 --> 00:59:54,352
Hey Mr. Harrington, can I be the one
to tell Peter he's expelled?

814
00:59:58,382 --> 01:00:04,492
The Washington Monument is 555 feet,
5 and one eigth inches tall.

815
01:00:05,542 --> 01:00:08,392
... mormont granite
are cut around the stone.

816
01:00:15,812 --> 01:00:17,812
No, no, no, no! Karen,
what's going on up there?

817
01:00:19,172 --> 01:00:22,852
<font color="#ff8040"><i>The Chitauri core has detonated and
caused severe structural damage to the elevator.</i></font>

818
01:00:23,332 --> 01:00:24,968
- My friends are up there.
- What?!

819
01:00:24,992 --> 01:00:27,068
Uh, don't worry, ma'am.
Everything's gonna be okay.

820
01:00:27,092 --> 01:00:29,612
Excuse me, excuse me!
Oh my God, that's tall!

821
01:00:35,032 --> 01:00:38,744
- Oh, my God. Look at the ceiling.
- Just stay calm everyone.

822
01:00:38,769 --> 01:00:40,852
We are going to die here.

823
01:00:42,777 --> 01:00:45,436
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Estimating 10 minutes
before catastrophic failure.</i></font>

824
01:00:45,452 --> 01:00:47,887
- We're freaking screwed.
- Okay, guys, I know that looks scary,

825
01:00:48,112 --> 01:00:50,572
but our safety systems are working.

826
01:00:50,592 --> 01:00:52,872
<i><font color="#ff8040">The safety systems
are completely failing.</font></i>

827
01:00:53,072 --> 01:00:57,092
- We're very safe in here.
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- The occupants are in imminent mortal danger.</i></font>

828
01:00:57,152 --> 01:00:59,152
I'm going as fast as I can!

829
01:01:10,192 --> 01:01:13,312
<font color="#ff8040"><i>You now have 125 seconds
until catastrophic failure.</i></font>

830
01:01:13,392 --> 01:01:17,222
- What? Why?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Unexpected motion has caused the deterioration to escalate.</i></font>

831
01:01:17,552 --> 01:01:20,832
- How do I get in there?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Activating Reconnaissance Drone.</i></font>

832
01:01:22,232 --> 01:01:24,592
Whoa. Has that been there this
whole time? That's awesome!

833
01:01:25,712 --> 01:01:28,152
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Locating optimal entry point.</i></font>

834
01:01:29,352 --> 01:01:32,152
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Proceed to southwest window.</i></font>
- Karen I'm on my way.

835
01:01:55,232 --> 01:01:57,792
Oh, God. Oh, God. Okay.

836
01:01:59,662 --> 01:02:02,192
<font color="#ff8040"><i>What's wrong? You've reached
the southwest window.</i></font>

837
01:02:02,192 --> 01:02:05,712
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Why are you hesitating?</i></font>
- It's just I've never been this high before.

838
01:02:05,752 --> 01:02:08,112
<font color="#ff8040"><i>You have also not
reinstalled your parachute,</i></font>

839
01:02:08,112 --> 01:02:10,752
<font color="#ff8040"><i>so a fall from this height
would most likely be lethal.</i></font>

840
01:02:12,312 --> 01:02:14,312
Alright.

841
01:02:17,182 --> 01:02:19,512
- Why is it not breaking?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- It's 4 inch ballistic glass.</i></font>

842
01:02:19,552 --> 01:02:21,552
<font color="#ff8040"><i>You'll have to create more momentum.</i></font>

843
01:02:40,952 --> 01:02:43,092
<i>DC metro police.
Identify yourself.</i>

844
01:02:43,172 --> 01:02:45,248
My friends are in there! Stop!

845
01:02:45,272 --> 01:02:47,272
<i>Return to the ground!
Immediately!</i>

846
01:02:47,352 --> 01:02:49,368
- Okay, who's next?
- Me! It's my turn!

847
01:02:49,392 --> 01:02:51,392
Flash, seriously?
What are you doing?

848
01:02:52,232 --> 01:02:54,312
Don't worry
about the trophy!

849
01:03:01,592 --> 01:03:05,152
<i>Stand down! Return to
the ground immediately!</i>

850
01:03:09,472 --> 01:03:11,912
<i>Return to the ground,
or we will open fire!</i>

851
01:03:12,072 --> 01:03:15,488
<i>- Go up, go up!</i>
- I got this.

852
01:03:15,512 --> 01:03:17,512
Take my trophy.

853
01:03:19,192 --> 01:03:21,192
This is your last chance.

854
01:03:21,632 --> 01:03:23,632
I'm gonna die.

855
01:03:46,912 --> 01:03:48,912
I did it!

856
01:04:02,032 --> 01:04:04,352
Hey, how you doing? Don't
worry about it, I got you.

857
01:04:04,392 --> 01:04:06,088
Yes! Yes!

858
01:04:06,112 --> 01:04:09,592
- Hey, hey, hey! Big guy, quit moving around!
- I'm sorry, sir! So sorry.

859
01:04:20,352 --> 01:04:22,352
- You can go.
- Okay.

860
01:04:22,452 --> 01:04:25,392
All right. This is your
stop. Go, go, go.

861
01:04:25,472 --> 01:04:28,072
Everybody out. Move
it people. Move it.

862
01:04:29,632 --> 01:04:31,632
Liz!

863
01:04:35,192 --> 01:04:37,192
You're okay. You're okay.

864
01:04:40,042 --> 01:04:44,232
- Okay.
- Good. Come on up, come on.

865
01:04:44,452 --> 01:04:47,152
- Guys, stand back.
- I got you.

866
01:04:47,862 --> 01:04:49,862
So, is everyone okay?

867
01:04:50,832 --> 01:04:52,832
<font color="#ff8040"><i>This is your chance, Peter.</i></font>

868
01:04:53,152 --> 01:04:55,152
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Kiss her.</i></font>

869
01:04:58,672 --> 01:05:00,672
Thank you.

870
01:05:03,452 --> 01:05:05,792
Are you really friends
with Peter Parker?

871
01:05:12,942 --> 01:05:14,942
I can finish the next order,

872
01:05:15,022 --> 01:05:17,232
but without any new
materials from that truck...

873
01:05:19,122 --> 01:05:21,122
Dammit...

874
01:05:21,422 --> 01:05:23,542
We're still enough to do the
Gargan deal though, right?

875
01:05:23,632 --> 01:05:25,632
Yeah. But then, that's it.

876
01:05:29,292 --> 01:05:32,032
Maybe it's time that I
build the high altitude seal.

877
01:05:32,102 --> 01:05:34,072
- Would you shut up about that?
- Look, one job...

878
01:05:34,114 --> 01:05:36,148
No.

879
01:05:37,072 --> 01:05:39,712
Eight years. Not a
word from the feds.

880
01:05:39,872 --> 01:05:44,032
Nothing from those halloween costume-
wearing bozos up there in Stark Tower.

881
01:05:44,692 --> 01:05:49,272
And then all of a sudden, this little
bastard in red tights shows up...

882
01:05:49,902 --> 01:05:52,552
And he thinks he can tear
down everything I built.

883
01:05:54,792 --> 01:05:56,792
Really?

884
01:06:00,408 --> 01:06:01,008
Found him.

885
01:06:01,232 --> 01:06:06,072
The Spider-Man swooped in, heroically
saving an academic decathlon team from Queens.

886
01:06:06,152 --> 01:06:09,232
The identity of the masked
hero is still unknown.

887
01:06:11,872 --> 01:06:13,872
Mom!

888
01:06:14,432 --> 01:06:16,552
Peter. Come here!

889
01:06:21,032 --> 01:06:25,336
<font color="#ffff00"><i>This past weekend, Midtown's academic
decathlon team defeated the country's best</i></font>

890
01:06:25,462 --> 01:06:28,672
<font color="#ffff00"><i>to win the national championship.
Later that day, they also defeated death.</i></font>

891
01:06:28,712 --> 01:06:31,512
<font color="#ffff00"><i>Explosives! Sally screamed!
Flash screamed, everybody screaming!</i></font>

892
01:06:31,592 --> 01:06:35,192
<font color="#ffff00"><i>There were purple lasers and smoke everywhere.
It was ****. Just like a Bon Jovi concert.</i></font>

893
01:06:35,302 --> 01:06:38,232
<font color="#ffff00"><i>As you know, we made it out alive.
And that's the important thing.</i></font>

894
01:06:38,912 --> 01:06:41,412
<font color="#ffff00"><i>I couldn't bear to lose a
student on a school trip.</i></font>

895
01:06:43,272 --> 01:06:46,912
<font color="#ffff00"><i>- Not again.
- Thankfully, no one was seriously injured.</i></font>

896
01:06:46,952 --> 01:06:50,848
<font color="#ffff00"><i>- Thanks to the Spider-Man.
- Thank you, Spider-Man.</i></font>

897
01:06:51,272 --> 01:06:54,312
<font color="#ffff00"><i>Up next:
The Spider-Man mania is sweeping the school.</i></font>

898
01:06:54,352 --> 01:06:56,632
<font color="#ffff00"><i>How can you show
your Spider spirit?</i></font>

899
01:07:00,752 --> 01:07:02,752
Dude, dude, dude...

900
01:07:02,772 --> 01:07:06,012
What is it like being famous
when nobody knows it's you?

901
01:07:06,032 --> 01:07:07,712
- Crazy, Ned.
- It is crazy!

902
01:07:07,712 --> 01:07:09,712
- Should we tell everyone?
- No.

903
01:07:10,032 --> 01:07:12,952
- Should I tell everyone?
- No, dude. That's not a good idea.

904
01:07:13,752 --> 01:07:15,752
- Okay. Well, we're gonna go to class.
- I'm not going to class.

905
01:07:16,112 --> 01:07:19,712
- But you're already in so much trouble for ditching the decathlon...
- Dude, listen, I figured it out, right...

906
01:07:19,712 --> 01:07:22,032
The wing suit guy is stealing
from Damage Control.

907
01:07:22,032 --> 01:07:26,592
And what he takes from Damage Control, that's
how he builds the weapons. All I gotta do is catch him!

908
01:07:26,992 --> 01:07:30,672
- But we have a Spanish quiz.
- Ned, I'm probably never gonna come back here.

909
01:07:31,032 --> 01:07:33,432
Mr. Stark is moving the
Avengers upstate, so...

910
01:07:34,132 --> 01:07:36,432
- when I bring this guy in...
- Dude!

911
01:07:36,602 --> 01:07:38,602
You wanna be a
high school dropout?

912
01:07:38,632 --> 01:07:41,032
I am so far beyond
high school right now.

913
01:07:41,352 --> 01:07:43,592
Parker! My office.

914
01:07:46,912 --> 01:07:51,472
So. You got detention.
You screwed up.

915
01:07:51,622 --> 01:07:55,002
You know what you did was wrong. The
question is, how are you gonna make things right?

916
01:07:55,132 --> 01:07:57,168
Maybe you were
trying to be cool.

917
01:07:57,192 --> 01:08:00,032
But take it from a guy who's
been frozen for 65 years.

918
01:08:00,192 --> 01:08:03,632
The only way to really be
cool, is to follow the rules.

919
01:08:04,272 --> 01:08:06,592
We all know what's right.
We all know what's wrong.

920
01:08:06,752 --> 01:08:09,832
Next time those turkeys try to convince you that something you know...

921
01:08:09,912 --> 01:08:12,032
Hey, where are you
going? Get back here!

922
01:08:12,372 --> 01:08:14,372
What would Captain America do?

923
01:08:14,552 --> 01:08:16,792
Why are you here? You
don't even have detention.

924
01:08:16,792 --> 01:08:20,792
Oh, I know. I just like coming
here to sketch people in crisis.

925
01:08:23,592 --> 01:08:26,128
It's you.

926
01:08:26,152 --> 01:08:29,872
So your body's changing. Believe
me, I know how that feels.

927
01:08:41,832 --> 01:08:43,332
May?

928
01:08:47,062 --> 01:08:50,032
- Hey, Karen, what's up?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Hey, Peter. How was your Spanish quiz?</i></font>

929
01:08:50,112 --> 01:08:52,952
Listen, I was wondering if you could help me.
I'm trying to figure out who the guys...

930
01:08:52,952 --> 01:08:56,472
under the bridge were that night, but, I mean
I can only kinda remember part of the license plate.

931
01:08:56,602 --> 01:08:59,152
<font color="#ff8040"><i>I can run facial recognition on
the footage of that encounter.</i></font>

932
01:08:59,152 --> 01:09:01,248
- Footage?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Yes, Peter.</i></font>

933
01:09:01,272 --> 01:09:03,650
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- I record everything you see.</i></font>
- Everything?

934
01:09:03,675 --> 01:09:05,774
- Everything.
- Like, all the time?

935
01:09:05,799 --> 01:09:09,672
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- It's called the Baby Monitor Protocol.</i></font>
- Yeah, of course, it is.

936
01:09:11,472 --> 01:09:14,532
- Yeah, just roll it back to last Friday.
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- With pleasure.</i></font>

937
01:09:14,572 --> 01:09:16,592
Hey, everyone! Yeah, kick-ass party.

938
01:09:16,592 --> 01:09:18,952
Hey, what's up, Liz?
Peter told me a lot about you.

939
01:09:19,092 --> 01:09:23,312
No, this is just me messing around.
Go later in the day...

940
01:09:23,312 --> 01:09:28,762
- It is I, Thor, son of Odin!
- No, no, no. That's definitely not what we wanna watch.

941
01:09:28,952 --> 01:09:32,568
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Your impressions are very funny.</i></font>
- Fast forward to the arms deal.

942
01:09:32,592 --> 01:09:35,568
Okay. The two on the right,
who are they?

943
01:09:35,592 --> 01:09:37,912
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Searching law enforcement databases...</i></font>

944
01:09:39,172 --> 01:09:42,392
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- No records found for two of the individuals.</i></font>
- Nothing?

945
01:09:42,432 --> 01:09:45,792
<font color="#ff8040"><i>One individual identified.
Aaron Davis, age 33.</i></font>

946
01:09:46,152 --> 01:09:50,548
<i><font color="#ff8040">- He has a criminal record. And an address here in Queens.</font></i>
- Let's pay him a visit.

947
01:09:50,572 --> 01:09:53,672
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Would you like me to activate the
Enhanced Interrogation Protocol?</i></font>

948
01:09:54,552 --> 01:09:55,752
Yeah.

949
01:10:10,302 --> 01:10:12,302
Remember me?

950
01:10:12,392 --> 01:10:14,792
I need information and you're
gonna give it to me now!

951
01:10:14,892 --> 01:10:16,892
- Alright, chill...
- Come on!

952
01:10:17,422 --> 01:10:19,792
- What happened to your voice?
- What do you mean, what happened to my voice?

953
01:10:20,032 --> 01:10:22,042
I heard you by the bridge.
I know what a girl sound like.

954
01:10:22,112 --> 01:10:25,568
I'm not a girl! I'm a boy!
I mean, I'm a man.

955
01:10:25,592 --> 01:10:29,288
- I don't care what you are. Boy, girl...
- I'm not a girl! I'm a man.

956
01:10:29,312 --> 01:10:31,752
Come on, man. Look, who
is selling these weapons?

957
01:10:31,992 --> 01:10:34,112
I need to know. Give
me names, or else.

958
01:10:37,452 --> 01:10:39,478
You ain't ever done
this before, huh?

959
01:10:39,502 --> 01:10:41,792
Deactivate interrogation mode.

960
01:10:43,582 --> 01:10:47,332
Look man, these guys are selling
weapons that are crazy dangerous.

961
01:10:47,372 --> 01:10:49,468
They can't just be
out on the streets.

962
01:10:49,492 --> 01:10:51,972
Look, if one of them can just
cut Delmar's bodega in half...

963
01:10:52,032 --> 01:10:54,432
- You know Delmar's?
- Yeah. The best sandwich in Queens.

964
01:10:54,712 --> 01:10:56,942
- The subhaven's pretty good.
- Nah, it's too much bread.

965
01:10:56,942 --> 01:10:59,872
- I like bread.
- Come on, man. Please.

966
01:11:01,552 --> 01:11:04,418
Stupid interrogation mode.
Karen, don't ever do that again.

967
01:11:04,442 --> 01:11:07,452
The other night, you told that dude
"if you're gonna shoot somebody, shoot me."

968
01:11:08,732 --> 01:11:10,178
That's pretty ballsy.

969
01:11:10,602 --> 01:11:13,872
I don't want those weapons in this neighborhood.
I got a nephew who live here.

970
01:11:15,342 --> 01:11:17,852
Who are these guys? What can you
tell me about the guy with the wings?

971
01:11:17,872 --> 01:11:20,952
Other than he's a psychopath
dressed like a demon? Nothing.

972
01:11:20,952 --> 01:11:23,592
I don't know who he is,
or where he is.

973
01:11:26,512 --> 01:11:28,512
I do know where
he's gonna be.

974
01:11:29,222 --> 01:11:33,392
- Really?
- Yeah, this crazy dude I used to work with. He's...

975
01:11:33,792 --> 01:11:36,898
- He's supposed to be doing a deal with him.
- Yes! Yeah!

976
01:11:38,712 --> 01:11:40,912
Hey. I didn't tell you where.
You don't have a location.

977
01:11:41,232 --> 01:11:43,752
Right. Of course. Yeah.
My bad. Silly. Just... Yeah.

978
01:11:45,932 --> 01:11:46,928
Where is it?

979
01:11:46,952 --> 01:11:51,312
Can I give you some advice? You
gotta get better at this part of the job.

980
01:11:51,392 --> 01:11:54,488
I don't understand.
I'm intimidating.

981
01:11:54,512 --> 01:11:57,552
- The Staten Island Ferry. 11:00.
- Oh, that's soon.

982
01:11:57,832 --> 01:11:59,832
Hey that's gonna
dissolve in two hours.

983
01:11:59,872 --> 01:12:01,492
No, no, no, no.
Come fix this.

984
01:12:01,492 --> 01:12:03,498
- Two hours. You deserve that.
- I got ice cream here, man.

985
01:12:03,523 --> 01:12:06,048
You deserve that, you're
a criminal. Bye, Mr. Criminal!

986
01:12:19,232 --> 01:12:20,632
Nice.

987
01:12:23,162 --> 01:12:25,832
Okay, Karen.
Activate Enhanced Reconnaissance mode.

988
01:12:25,992 --> 01:12:29,292
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Sure thing.</i></font>
- He's out front. Main deck.

989
01:12:29,392 --> 01:12:32,128
- I hate this guy.
- That's the guy from the bridge, right?

990
01:12:32,152 --> 01:12:34,288
- Who's that other guy?
- Just keep me posted.

991
01:12:34,312 --> 01:12:36,512
<font color="#ff8040"><i>There's no record of him
in my criminal database.</i></font>

992
01:12:36,742 --> 01:12:39,152
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Incoming call from May Parker.
Shall I reroute to your heads-up display?</i></font>

993
01:12:39,192 --> 01:12:41,092
I can't talk right now.
I'll call her back.

994
01:12:42,072 --> 01:12:44,282
Hey, Droney.
Keep an eye on that guy.

995
01:12:44,312 --> 01:12:46,312
We can't let anybody
get away this time.

996
01:12:54,162 --> 01:12:56,162
- Who's the guy on the left?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Mac Gargan.</i></font>

997
01:12:56,312 --> 01:12:58,592
<i><font color="#ff8040">Extensive criminal
record including homicide.</font></i>

998
01:12:58,812 --> 01:13:00,688
<i><font color="#ff8040">Would you like me
to activate Instant Kill?</font></i>

999
01:13:00,712 --> 01:13:03,132
No, Karen.
Stop it with the Instant Kill already!

1000
01:13:05,012 --> 01:13:07,012
White pick-up truck.

1001
01:13:10,982 --> 01:13:13,712
Droney, scan the ship
for a white pick-up truck.

1002
01:13:32,522 --> 01:13:35,792
This is too perfect. They got the
weapons, the buyers, and the sellers all in one place.

1003
01:13:35,872 --> 01:13:37,992
<font color="#ff8040"><i>Incoming call from Tony Stark.</i></font>

1004
01:13:38,012 --> 01:13:39,832
- No, no, no. Don't answer!
- Mr. Parker.

1005
01:13:40,072 --> 01:13:42,552
- Got a sec?
- Uhh, I'm actually at school.

1006
01:13:42,592 --> 01:13:45,112
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- No, you're not.</i></font>
- Nice work in DC...

1007
01:13:45,432 --> 01:13:50,088
My Dad never really gave me a lot of support.
Now I'm just trying to break the cycle of chain...

1008
01:13:50,112 --> 01:13:52,792
- I'm kind of in the middle of something right now...
- Don't cut me off when I'm complimenting you.

1009
01:13:52,792 --> 01:13:55,352
Anyway. Great things
are about to happen... What is that?

1010
01:13:56,592 --> 01:13:57,792
I'm at band practice...

1011
01:13:58,222 --> 01:14:01,952
That's odd. Happy told me
you quit band six weeks ago.

1012
01:14:01,952 --> 01:14:04,172
- What's up?
- I got to go. End call!

1013
01:14:04,872 --> 01:14:06,872
I'll take those!

1014
01:14:09,392 --> 01:14:11,572
Hey guys. The illegal weapons
deal ferry was at 10:30.

1015
01:14:11,592 --> 01:14:12,992
You missed it.

1016
01:14:20,832 --> 01:14:22,232
Spider-guy's here.

1017
01:14:25,072 --> 01:14:27,072
Whoa, whoa,
not so fast!

1018
01:14:28,042 --> 01:14:30,352
Are you guys okay? My
bad. That was a little hard.

1019
01:14:31,632 --> 01:14:33,832
I gotta say, the other guy was
way better with that thing.

1020
01:14:35,072 --> 01:14:37,472
And honestly,
I'm,  I'm shocked.

1021
01:14:49,312 --> 01:14:52,752
Freeze! FBI! Get
on the ground!

1022
01:14:52,812 --> 01:14:55,632
- What do you mean, FBI?
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- The FBI is the Federal Bureau of Investigation...</i></font>

1023
01:14:55,632 --> 01:14:57,872
I know what the FBI means,
but what are they doing here?

1024
01:15:04,712 --> 01:15:07,052
Get outta the way!
Get outta the way!

1025
01:15:10,952 --> 01:15:12,772
Look out, look out!
Move, move, move!

1026
01:15:18,672 --> 01:15:21,272
Get to the top deck.
We're getting out of here.

1027
01:15:57,232 --> 01:15:58,832
Activate taser web!

1028
01:16:09,822 --> 01:16:12,352
You're messing with things
you don't understand.

1029
01:16:52,132 --> 01:16:53,892
Oh, my God!
What do I do?

1030
01:16:54,042 --> 01:16:57,342
Karen, give me an x-ray of the
boat and target all the strongest points.

1031
01:17:01,102 --> 01:17:03,102
Web grenade.
Web grenade!

1032
01:17:05,632 --> 01:17:07,432
Splitter web.

1033
01:17:37,882 --> 01:17:42,488
<font color="#ff8040"><i>- Great job, Peter. You're 98% successful.</i></font>
- 98?

1034
01:17:42,512 --> 01:17:44,512
Yeah, Spider-Man!

1035
01:17:46,912 --> 01:17:48,912
No, no, no!

1036
01:18:08,512 --> 01:18:10,512
No!

1037
01:18:26,952 --> 01:18:28,752
What the hell?

1038
01:18:32,072 --> 01:18:34,072
What the hell?

1039
01:18:36,312 --> 01:18:40,172
Hi, Spider-Man...
"Band practice", was it?

1040
01:19:04,512 --> 01:19:06,512
Yeah, Iron Man!

1041
01:19:14,752 --> 01:19:16,372
Uhh, Mr. Stark?

1042
01:19:18,632 --> 01:19:19,848
Hey..  Mr. Stark, can i do anything?

1043
01:19:19,872 --> 01:19:21,572
What do you want me to do?

1044
01:19:23,162 --> 01:19:25,602
I think you've done enough.

1045
01:19:40,902 --> 01:19:43,672
So that's it? You're
just gonna run?

1046
01:19:46,852 --> 01:19:48,852
Feds were waiting for us.

1047
01:19:49,562 --> 01:19:51,592
And now, we're on Iron Man's radar?

1048
01:19:53,232 --> 01:19:55,232
Yeah, I'm running.

1049
01:19:56,402 --> 01:19:59,968
- You should, too.
- You know I can't do that.

1050
01:19:59,992 --> 01:20:03,128
- So now, what?
- Mason.

1051
01:20:03,552 --> 01:20:07,032
Can you get that high altitude
seal up and running in time?

1052
01:20:08,112 --> 01:20:10,808
Seriously?
Yes.

1053
01:20:10,832 --> 01:20:12,232
You will not regret this.

1054
01:20:15,752 --> 01:20:17,352
You in?

1055
01:20:29,032 --> 01:20:32,952
Previously on "Peter screws the Pooch,"
I thought you'd stayed away from this,

1056
01:20:33,202 --> 01:20:37,852
instead, you hacked a multi-million
dollar suit so you could sneak around,

1057
01:20:37,852 --> 01:20:42,022
behind my back, doing the
one thing I told you not to do.

1058
01:20:42,532 --> 01:20:46,162
- Is everyone okay?
- No thanks to you.

1059
01:20:47,812 --> 01:20:49,812
No thanks to me?

1060
01:20:52,042 --> 01:20:55,792
Those weapons were out there and I
tried to tell you about it, but you didn't listen.

1061
01:20:56,672 --> 01:20:59,512
None of this would've happened
if you had just listened to me.

1062
01:21:00,392 --> 01:21:02,632
If you even cared,
you'd actually be here.

1063
01:21:07,712 --> 01:21:10,672
I did listen, kid.
Who do you think called the FBI, huh?

1064
01:21:11,322 --> 01:21:14,032
Do you know that I was the
only one who believed in you?

1065
01:21:14,132 --> 01:21:18,332
Everyone else said I was crazy
to recruit a 14-year old kid.

1066
01:21:18,472 --> 01:21:19,292
I'm 15.

1067
01:21:19,371 --> 01:21:21,908
No, this is where you zip it! All right?
The adult is talking.

1068
01:21:22,332 --> 01:21:26,512
What if somebody had died tonight?
Different story, right? 'Cause that's on you.

1069
01:21:27,472 --> 01:21:30,992
And if you died...
I feel like that's on me.

1070
01:21:31,822 --> 01:21:34,697
- I don't need that on my conscience.
- Yes, sir... I'm sorry, I...

1071
01:21:34,722 --> 01:21:39,328
- Sorry doesn't cut it.
- I understand. I just wanted to be like you.

1072
01:21:39,352 --> 01:21:41,352
And I wanted
you to be better.

1073
01:21:42,412 --> 01:21:44,412
Okay. It's not working out.
I'm gonna need the suit back.

1074
01:21:44,412 --> 01:21:46,508
- For how long?
- Forever.

1075
01:21:46,932 --> 01:21:48,932
No. No, no, no.
Please...

1076
01:21:49,012 --> 01:21:50,048
- Let's have it.
- You don't understand...

1077
01:21:50,072 --> 01:21:52,292
This is all I have.
I'm nothing without this suit.

1078
01:21:52,952 --> 01:21:56,792
If you're nothing without this
suit, then you shouldn't have it. Okay?

1079
01:21:56,882 --> 01:21:59,082
Gosh, I sound like my dad.

1080
01:22:01,072 --> 01:22:03,072
I don't have
any other clothes.

1081
01:22:03,472 --> 01:22:05,472
Okay. We'll sort that out.

1082
01:22:21,042 --> 01:22:24,032
I've been calling you all day.
But you don't answer your phone.

1083
01:22:24,112 --> 01:22:27,872
You can't do that.
Then this ferry thing happens...

1084
01:22:28,672 --> 01:22:31,712
I've called five
police stations.

1085
01:22:31,792 --> 01:22:34,992
Five. I called 5 of your
friends. I called Ned's mother.

1086
01:22:35,112 --> 01:22:38,032
I'm fine. May, I'm okay.
Honestly, just relax. I'm fine.

1087
01:22:39,042 --> 01:22:42,212
Cut the bullshit.
I know you left detention.

1088
01:22:42,212 --> 01:22:44,512
I know you left the hotel
room in Washington.

1089
01:22:44,592 --> 01:22:48,142
I know you sneak out of this
house every night. There's no fine.

1090
01:22:48,142 --> 01:22:50,152
Peter, you have to tell
me what's going on.

1091
01:22:50,352 --> 01:22:52,672
Just lay it out. It's
just me and you.

1092
01:22:54,472 --> 01:22:56,472
I lost the Stark internship.

1093
01:22:56,492 --> 01:22:58,588
- What?
- Yeah.

1094
01:22:58,612 --> 01:23:00,488
What happened?

1095
01:23:00,512 --> 01:23:04,072
I just said that I could work really hard,
and he could, he would, you know...

1096
01:23:05,432 --> 01:23:07,492
But... I screwed it up.

1097
01:23:07,592 --> 01:23:09,592
That's okay. It's okay.

1098
01:23:11,072 --> 01:23:12,972
It's okay...

1099
01:23:13,232 --> 01:23:15,232
I'm sorry I made you worry.

1100
01:23:15,672 --> 01:23:18,792
- You know I'm not trying to ruin your life.
- Yeah, I know.

1101
01:23:20,432 --> 01:23:22,512
- I used to sneak out, too.
- Yeah?

1102
01:23:25,622 --> 01:23:30,568
And take a shower. You smell...
smell like garbage.

1103
01:23:30,592 --> 01:23:32,592
I know.

1104
01:23:35,312 --> 01:23:37,632
Peter, you're a good kid,
and you're a smart kid.

1105
01:23:37,632 --> 01:23:39,632
So just try to keep your
head straight, okay?

1106
01:23:40,512 --> 01:23:44,272
- Okay.
- Alright. Get out of here.

1107
01:23:51,672 --> 01:23:54,633
Are you expelled? Do you have to
go to that high school on 46th,

1108
01:23:54,658 --> 01:23:58,832
- where the principal has a crossbow?
- Pretty sure that's an urban myth, but no, I'm not expelled.

1109
01:23:59,432 --> 01:24:01,432
You're so lucky.

1110
01:24:49,392 --> 01:24:50,078
Hey.

1111
01:24:50,102 --> 01:24:52,152
Hey.. I thought you had
Calculus, fifth period.

1112
01:24:52,472 --> 01:24:54,592
Yeah, I'm just dipped
on Homecoming stuff.

1113
01:24:55,142 --> 01:24:57,142
Hey, look. I, uhh...

1114
01:24:57,552 --> 01:25:01,352
- I just wanted to apologize about the whole decathlon thing.
- It's fine.

1115
01:25:01,752 --> 01:25:04,652
Last week, decathlon was
the most important thing, but...

1116
01:25:04,712 --> 01:25:06,512
I almost died.

1117
01:25:07,482 --> 01:25:09,482
No. I just mean that...

1118
01:25:09,752 --> 01:25:11,952
It was not cool, especially...

1119
01:25:14,232 --> 01:25:16,132
Because...

1120
01:25:17,152 --> 01:25:19,472
... I like you.

1121
01:25:19,942 --> 01:25:21,942
I know.

1122
01:25:24,172 --> 01:25:27,772
- You do?
- You're terrible at keeping secrets.

1123
01:25:27,802 --> 01:25:29,802
Yeah, you'd be surprised.

1124
01:25:32,512 --> 01:25:34,792
I, I gotta get to class, but, umm...

1125
01:25:35,112 --> 01:25:38,752
I'd say we should hang out, but
I'm gonna be in detention for a bit...

1126
01:25:39,672 --> 01:25:41,672
Ever... But, umm...

1127
01:25:42,592 --> 01:25:44,852
I guess you already have
a date for Homecoming.

1128
01:25:44,862 --> 01:25:47,042
Actually, I'm so busy planning it,

1129
01:25:47,042 --> 01:25:49,042
I never really got around to that part, so...

1130
01:25:50,512 --> 01:25:55,118
- You wanna, go with me?
- Yeah.

1131
01:25:55,142 --> 01:25:57,142
- Sure.
- Really?

1132
01:25:57,232 --> 01:25:59,232
I mean, uhh... Great. Cool.

1133
01:25:59,272 --> 01:26:03,752
- Cool.
- I'm actually, going that way.

1134
01:26:14,952 --> 01:26:16,952
May, I need your help!

1135
01:26:50,952 --> 01:26:53,212
It's game day. So...
What's the plan?

1136
01:26:53,272 --> 01:26:55,952
Open the door for her.
Tell her she looks nice.

1137
01:26:55,952 --> 01:26:58,648
But not too much because that's creepy.
No. And, uhh...

1138
01:26:58,672 --> 01:27:01,552
When I dance with her, I'll
put my hands on her hips.

1139
01:27:01,672 --> 01:27:03,472
Your daffodils.

1140
01:27:05,832 --> 01:27:07,832
- Love you.
- Bye.

1141
01:27:21,832 --> 01:27:25,528
- You must be Peter.
- Yeah.

1142
01:27:25,552 --> 01:27:29,248
I'm Liz' Dad.
Put her there.

1143
01:27:29,272 --> 01:27:33,102
Hell of a grip! Come on in here.
Come on.

1144
01:27:58,192 --> 01:28:00,092
Hi, Peter.

1145
01:28:00,152 --> 01:28:02,432
- You look very handsome.
- Thank you.

1146
01:28:04,072 --> 01:28:06,072
You got his name, right?

1147
01:28:06,072 --> 01:28:08,168
- Freddy?
- Peter.

1148
01:28:08,192 --> 01:28:10,192
Peter. Peter.

1149
01:28:10,492 --> 01:28:13,702
- I'm gonna go get Liz.
- Okay.

1150
01:28:19,792 --> 01:28:22,232
- You all right, Pete?
- Yeah.

1151
01:28:22,632 --> 01:28:25,992
Because you
look... pale.

1152
01:28:27,042 --> 01:28:30,992
You want something to drink, like a Bourbon,
or Scotch, or something like that?

1153
01:28:31,112 --> 01:28:34,712
- I'm not old enough to drink.
- That's the right answer.

1154
01:28:37,012 --> 01:28:40,012
Wow! Wow, wow, wow,
do you look beautiful.

1155
01:28:40,032 --> 01:28:43,048
- Please don't embarass me, Dad.
- Doesn't she, Pete?

1156
01:28:43,072 --> 01:28:45,352
Yeah, you look really good.

1157
01:28:46,352 --> 01:28:48,352
Once again, that's
the right answer.

1158
01:28:48,502 --> 01:28:54,008
- Is that a corsage?
- Thanks.

1159
01:28:54,432 --> 01:28:58,122
Well, hey, I'm your chauffeur, so
let's get this show on the road.

1160
01:28:58,132 --> 01:29:00,132
No, no, no. We have to
take some pictures, Babe.

1161
01:29:01,312 --> 01:29:04,008
Right here.
Perfect. Okay...

1162
01:29:04,032 --> 01:29:07,862
Come on, you guys.
Peter, closer.

1163
01:29:10,082 --> 01:29:11,682
Smile!

1164
01:29:12,392 --> 01:29:14,392
There you go.

1165
01:29:20,392 --> 01:29:23,908
- Sir, you don't have to drive us..
- Nah nah. It's not a big deal.

1166
01:29:23,932 --> 01:29:26,022
I'm going out of town.
It's right on my way.

1167
01:29:26,022 --> 01:29:28,272
- He's always coming and going.
- Last time, Babe.

1168
01:29:28,792 --> 01:29:29,992
- Thank you.
- I promise.

1169
01:29:30,012 --> 01:29:31,412
- He's cute!
- Sst..!

1170
01:29:33,542 --> 01:29:35,542
- See you in a couple of days.
- Okay.

1171
01:29:36,372 --> 01:29:38,208
Come on, Pedro.

1172
01:29:38,232 --> 01:29:40,312
- Bye, Peter. Have fun.
- Yeah, I will.

1173
01:29:51,192 --> 01:29:54,028
- What are you gonna do, Pete?
- What?

1174
01:29:54,052 --> 01:29:56,088
When you graduate. What
do you think you're gonna do?

1175
01:29:56,112 --> 01:29:59,488
- Oh. Umm, I don't know
- Don't grill him, Dad.

1176
01:29:59,512 --> 01:30:01,512
Just sayin'.
You know.

1177
01:30:02,112 --> 01:30:06,192
While you guys are going to that school,
you pretty much have your life planned out, right?

1178
01:30:07,152 --> 01:30:09,152
Yeah... No, I'm just a sophomore.

1179
01:30:09,632 --> 01:30:11,632
Peter has an internship
with Tony Stark, so...

1180
01:30:12,202 --> 01:30:15,031
- I think he doesn't have to worry.
- Really?

1181
01:30:15,056 --> 01:30:17,512
- Stark?
- So cool.

1182
01:30:18,832 --> 01:30:20,832
What do you do?

1183
01:30:20,872 --> 01:30:23,592
Yeah, actually, I don't
intern for him anymore.

1184
01:30:23,832 --> 01:30:26,528
- Seriously?
- Yeah. It got, umm...

1185
01:30:26,552 --> 01:30:29,248
- Boring.
- It was boring?

1186
01:30:29,272 --> 01:30:33,312
- You got to hang out with Spider-Man.
- Really? Spider-Man?

1187
01:30:34,152 --> 01:30:37,232
Wow. What's he like?

1188
01:30:37,522 --> 01:30:40,432
Yeah, he's nice.
Nice man.

1189
01:30:41,222 --> 01:30:43,122
Solid dude.

1190
01:30:46,552 --> 01:30:48,792
- Look! So cute.
- Aww.

1191
01:30:54,312 --> 01:30:57,032
I've seen you around,
right? I mean...

1192
01:30:57,452 --> 01:31:00,782
Somewhere. We've, uhh... Have
we ever? Because even the voice...

1193
01:31:01,472 --> 01:31:03,472
He does academic
decathlon, I think.

1194
01:31:03,952 --> 01:31:08,032
- And he was at my party.
- It was a great party! Really great, yeah.

1195
01:31:08,592 --> 01:31:10,952
Beautiful house.
Lot of windows.

1196
01:31:11,202 --> 01:31:16,192
- You were there for like, 2 seconds.
- That was... I was there longer than 2 seconds.

1197
01:31:16,872 --> 01:31:20,192
- You disappeared.
- No. No, I did not disappear.

1198
01:31:20,652 --> 01:31:24,212
Yes, you did, you disappeared like
you always do. Like you did in DC, too.

1199
01:31:33,552 --> 01:31:36,392
That was terrible, what happened
down there in DC, though.

1200
01:31:36,832 --> 01:31:38,832
Were you scared?

1201
01:31:39,352 --> 01:31:43,952
I bet you were glad when your old pal Spider-Man
showed up in the elevator though, huh?

1202
01:31:47,352 --> 01:31:49,352
Yeah, well, I... I
actually didn't go up.

1203
01:31:49,472 --> 01:31:51,472
I saw it all
from the ground.

1204
01:31:53,342 --> 01:31:55,392
Pretty lucky that he
was there that day.

1205
01:31:59,552 --> 01:32:02,032
Good ol' Spider-Man.

1206
01:32:06,042 --> 01:32:08,042
Dad. The light.

1207
01:32:23,972 --> 01:32:25,468
Here we are.

1208
01:32:25,492 --> 01:32:27,492
- End of the line.
- Thanks, Dad.

1209
01:32:28,382 --> 01:32:33,072
You head in there, Gumdrop. I'm
gonna give Peter the, "Dad talk".

1210
01:32:34,902 --> 01:32:36,928
Don't let him
intimidate you.

1211
01:32:36,952 --> 01:32:38,951
- Love you.
- Love you, Gumdrop.

1212
01:32:38,976 --> 01:32:40,420
Have a safe flight.

1213
01:32:43,172 --> 01:32:45,172
You look so pretty!

1214
01:32:49,842 --> 01:32:52,968
- Does she know?
- Know what?

1215
01:32:53,392 --> 01:32:56,808
So she doesn't. Good.
Close to the vest.

1216
01:32:56,832 --> 01:33:00,272
I admire that. I got a
few secrets of my own.

1217
01:33:00,952 --> 01:33:04,032
Of all the reasons I didn't
want my daughter to date...

1218
01:33:06,702 --> 01:33:10,672
Peter, nothing is more
important than family.

1219
01:33:10,672 --> 01:33:14,052
You saved my daughter's life and I
could never forget something like that.

1220
01:33:14,152 --> 01:33:17,192
So I'm gonna give you
one chance. Are you ready?

1221
01:33:17,872 --> 01:33:21,192
You walk through those doors,
you forget any of this happened.

1222
01:33:21,252 --> 01:33:24,552
And don't you ever, ever...

1223
01:33:24,752 --> 01:33:27,152
Interfere with
my business again.

1224
01:33:27,472 --> 01:33:29,372
Because if you do...

1225
01:33:29,432 --> 01:33:31,432
I'll kill you...

1226
01:33:31,802 --> 01:33:33,802
And everybody you love.

1227
01:33:34,542 --> 01:33:38,242
I'll kill you dead. That's what I
I'll do to protect my family, Pete.

1228
01:33:38,242 --> 01:33:40,242
You understand?

1229
01:33:40,894 --> 01:33:41,894
Hey.

1230
01:33:43,492 --> 01:33:45,692
I just saved your life.

1231
01:33:45,872 --> 01:33:50,458
- Now, what do you say?
- Thank you.

1232
01:33:50,482 --> 01:33:52,282
You're welcome.

1233
01:33:52,372 --> 01:33:56,942
Now, you go in there, and you
show my daughter a good time.

1234
01:33:56,942 --> 01:34:00,472
Okay?
Just not too good.

1235
01:34:55,582 --> 01:34:57,582
What did he say to you?

1236
01:35:01,072 --> 01:35:03,072
I gotta go.

1237
01:35:04,322 --> 01:35:08,392
I'm sorry.
You don't deserve this.

1238
01:35:28,852 --> 01:35:31,302
He gave you a choice.
You chose wrong.

1239
01:35:31,327 --> 01:35:34,672
- What the hell?
- What's with the crappy costume?

1240
01:35:36,552 --> 01:35:38,352
My web shooters.

1241
01:35:46,472 --> 01:35:48,952
I wasn't sure about this
thing at first, but...

1242
01:35:49,712 --> 01:35:51,312
Damn!

1243
01:35:56,192 --> 01:35:57,792
Gross!

1244
01:36:08,072 --> 01:36:11,762
- Why did he send you here?
- Guess you'll never know.

1245
01:36:15,902 --> 01:36:17,502
Nice shot!

1246
01:36:23,832 --> 01:36:26,012
Ned, the guy with
the wings is Liz' Dad.

1247
01:36:26,072 --> 01:36:27,948
- What?
- I know. I gotta tell Mr. Stark.

1248
01:36:27,972 --> 01:36:30,316
Call Happy Hogan. He's
Mr. Stark's head of security.

1249
01:36:30,392 --> 01:36:32,492
And get a computer
and track my phone for me.

1250
01:36:32,572 --> 01:36:35,192
- Are you gonna be okay?
- Hurry, we gotta catch him before he leaves town!

1251
01:36:36,552 --> 01:36:38,552
I'm sorry about dinner, but...

1252
01:36:39,042 --> 01:36:41,732
I know when Branzino's fresh.
And that was not fresh, okay?

1253
01:36:41,732 --> 01:36:43,148
So...

1254
01:36:43,172 --> 01:36:45,172
Flash, I need your
car and your phone.

1255
01:36:45,352 --> 01:36:48,502
Sir, technically this is my dad's car, sir.
So I can't...

1256
01:36:56,802 --> 01:37:00,168
- Hello, Ned? Hey, hey, hey. Can you hear me?
- Go for Ned.

1257
01:37:00,192 --> 01:37:02,142
Ned. I need you to
track my phone for me.

1258
01:37:02,172 --> 01:37:04,172
Yeah, but where is it?

1259
01:37:07,992 --> 01:37:10,312
Genius move. Okay, he just passed
a Gamestop on Jackson Avenue.

1260
01:37:10,392 --> 01:37:13,572
Hey, where are the headlights
on this thing? I'm in Flash's car.

1261
01:37:13,572 --> 01:37:15,982
- I'll pull the specs.
- Okay, you're on speaker phone.

1262
01:37:15,992 --> 01:37:18,112
You stole Flash's car?
Awesome.

1263
01:37:18,112 --> 01:37:22,437
Yeah, it's awesome! Get outta
the way, outta the way! Move!

1264
01:37:22,532 --> 01:37:24,408
- Peter, you okay?
- I've never really driven before.

1265
01:37:24,432 --> 01:37:27,652
Only in parking lots.
This is a huge step up!

1266
01:37:29,762 --> 01:37:31,852
- Hey, have you gotten through to Happy yet?
- Yeah, I'm working on it.

1267
01:37:31,852 --> 01:37:33,852
I just gotta battle through
the phone system.

1268
01:37:37,672 --> 01:37:39,672
Guy in the chair!

1269
01:37:44,002 --> 01:37:45,932
Takeoff in 9 minutes! Hello?

1270
01:37:45,932 --> 01:37:48,152
- Hello? Who is this?
- Mr. Happy, it's Ned.

1271
01:37:48,152 --> 01:37:50,198
- Who?
- I'm an associate of Peter Parker.

1272
01:37:50,222 --> 01:37:52,592
- He has something very important to tell you...
- You gotta be shitting me.

1273
01:37:53,922 --> 01:37:56,842
- Damn!
- Hey, Ned. How are we going on with those headlights?

1274
01:37:58,512 --> 01:38:00,572
Round knob,
to the left of the steering wheel

1275
01:38:00,572 --> 01:38:02,598
- turn it clockwise.
- Left? Okay.

1276
01:38:03,022 --> 01:38:06,032
Okay, perfect. So where's
my phone now?

1277
01:38:06,092 --> 01:38:09,152
- He stopped in an old industrial park in Brooklyn.
- What? That makes no sense.

1278
01:38:09,152 --> 01:38:12,968
- I thought he said he was going out of town.
- Weird. Oh, I reached Mr. Happy.

1279
01:38:12,992 --> 01:38:15,732
Don't think he likes you, by the way.
It sounded like he was catching a flight.

1280
01:38:15,752 --> 01:38:17,792
- He said something about taking off in 9 minutes.
- What?

1281
01:38:17,792 --> 01:38:20,052
- He was surrounded by a bunch of boxes.
- Boxes?

1282
01:38:20,052 --> 01:38:22,052
It's moving day!

1283
01:38:22,132 --> 01:38:24,392
He's gonna rob that plane!
I gotta stop him.

1284
01:38:28,072 --> 01:38:30,072
All right. Wheels
up in 8 minutes.

1285
01:38:30,122 --> 01:38:32,872
We just gotta load Tony's
old Hulkbuster armor,

1286
01:38:32,912 --> 01:38:34,912
prototype for
Cap's new shield,

1287
01:38:34,992 --> 01:38:38,028
and the Megging...
the Meg...

1288
01:38:38,052 --> 01:38:40,052
Thor's magic belt.

1289
01:38:40,552 --> 01:38:43,288
Okay, slow down. You're
getting close. It's on your right.

1290
01:38:43,312 --> 01:38:45,312
- What?
- Turn right. Turn right!

1291
01:38:53,832 --> 01:38:56,178
- Peter! Are you okay?
- Yeah.

1292
01:38:56,202 --> 01:38:58,202
Just keep trying to
get through to Happy.

1293
01:38:59,072 --> 01:39:01,072
It's been an honor, Spider-Man.

1294
01:39:01,452 --> 01:39:03,452
What are you doing here?
There's a dance.

1295
01:39:07,712 --> 01:39:12,832
I'm... looking... at porn.

1296
01:39:51,622 --> 01:39:55,366
- Surprised?
- Oh, hey, Pete.

1297
01:39:55,752 --> 01:39:59,272
- I didn't hear you come in.
- It's over. I've got you.

1298
01:39:59,352 --> 01:40:01,958
Y'know, I gotta tell you, Pete...

1299
01:40:01,982 --> 01:40:04,532
I really, really admire your grit.

1300
01:40:06,212 --> 01:40:08,212
I see why Liz likes you.

1301
01:40:09,412 --> 01:40:12,399
I do. When you first came
into the house, I wasn't sure.

1302
01:40:12,424 --> 01:40:15,248
I thought, "really?"
But I get it now.

1303
01:40:15,272 --> 01:40:18,128
- How could you do this to her?
- To her?

1304
01:40:18,152 --> 01:40:20,912
I'm not doing anything to her,
Pete. I'm doing this, for her.

1305
01:40:21,032 --> 01:40:23,032
Hmm. Yeah.

1306
01:40:26,892 --> 01:40:28,892
Peter.

1307
01:40:29,442 --> 01:40:33,102
You're young. You don't
understand how the world works.

1308
01:40:33,102 --> 01:40:36,152
Yeah, but I understand that selling
weapons to criminals is wrong.

1309
01:40:36,202 --> 01:40:38,732
How do you think your buddy
Stark paid for that tower?

1310
01:40:38,792 --> 01:40:43,832
Or any of his little toys? Those people,
Pete, those people up there, the rich and powerful...

1311
01:40:44,672 --> 01:40:47,258
They do whatever they
want. Guys like us...

1312
01:40:47,282 --> 01:40:49,282
Like you and me...

1313
01:40:49,632 --> 01:40:52,648
They don't care about us.
We build their roads,

1314
01:40:52,672 --> 01:40:56,332
and we fight all their wars and
everything, but they don't care about us.

1315
01:40:56,392 --> 01:40:59,862
We have to pick up after them.
We have to eat their table scraps.

1316
01:41:02,082 --> 01:41:03,782
That's how it is.

1317
01:41:04,702 --> 01:41:06,822
I know you know what
I'm talking about, Peter.

1318
01:41:06,832 --> 01:41:08,832
Why are you
telling me this?

1319
01:41:08,902 --> 01:41:10,962
Because I want
you to understand.

1320
01:41:11,372 --> 01:41:15,532
And... I needed a little
time to get her airborne.

1321
01:41:29,552 --> 01:41:31,552
I'm sorry, Peter.

1322
01:41:34,332 --> 01:41:37,622
What are you talking about? That
thing hasn't even touched me yet.

1323
01:41:38,812 --> 01:41:40,812
True. But then again...

1324
01:41:41,012 --> 01:41:43,052
It wasn't really trying to.

1325
01:41:49,322 --> 01:41:51,492
- Chief, they're powering those engines. C'mon.
- Okay.

1326
01:41:51,782 --> 01:41:53,782
Yeah. Yeah.

1327
01:42:46,742 --> 01:42:48,742
Okay, ready?

1328
01:42:57,712 --> 01:42:59,712
Hello?!

1329
01:43:02,222 --> 01:43:05,482
Hello!!
Please...

1330
01:43:05,682 --> 01:43:08,632
Hey, please...
I'm down here!

1331
01:43:08,632 --> 01:43:11,552
I'm down here! I'm stuck.
I'm stuck! I can't move...

1332
01:43:11,852 --> 01:43:13,852
I can't...

1333
01:43:30,412 --> 01:43:32,432
If you're nothing
without this suit,

1334
01:43:32,552 --> 01:43:34,552
then you shouldn't have it.

1335
01:43:40,422 --> 01:43:44,288
Come on, Peter.
Come on, Spider-Man.

1336
01:43:44,312 --> 01:43:46,408
Come on, Spider-Man.

1337
01:43:46,432 --> 01:43:48,432
Come on, Spider-Man.

1338
01:43:50,592 --> 01:43:52,592
Come on, Spider-Man!

1339
01:44:45,552 --> 01:44:47,352
Launch for intercept.
Green light. Green light.

1340
01:44:47,392 --> 01:44:49,392
Oh, yeah.

1341
01:45:03,152 --> 01:45:05,552
Retro-reflective panels engaged.

1342
01:45:17,252 --> 01:45:20,272
Got a visual on the plane,
but feeling little resistance.

1343
01:45:20,292 --> 01:45:22,292
It's probably just drag
on the new turbines.

1344
01:45:35,602 --> 01:45:37,952
Look out for the cloaking camera.
Stay on the blindspots.

1345
01:45:48,102 --> 01:45:50,102
Oh, my God.
Oh, my God.

1346
01:45:50,412 --> 01:45:52,762
Deploy high altitude
vacuum seal.

1347
01:45:52,762 --> 01:45:54,762
This better work, Mason.

1348
01:45:59,912 --> 01:46:02,962
Trust me, boss. Even one of those
boxes, and we are set for life.

1349
01:46:02,962 --> 01:46:04,962
Yeah.

1350
01:46:15,892 --> 01:46:18,952
You have 30 seconds to get to the
cockpit and override their security.

1351
01:46:30,852 --> 01:46:34,332
- Cloning transponder signal.
- Launching decoy drone.

1352
01:46:38,282 --> 01:46:40,282
Entering new coordinates.

1353
01:46:46,112 --> 01:46:48,312
- Good. So it's on its way?
- Yes, sir. Right on course.

1354
01:46:48,312 --> 01:46:50,312
Okay. Thank you.

1355
01:46:50,822 --> 01:46:52,822
All right.

1356
01:47:04,752 --> 01:47:06,752
Hot dog.

1357
01:47:55,972 --> 01:47:58,048
Just a typical
Homecoming...

1358
01:47:58,072 --> 01:48:00,192
on the outside
of an invisible jet...

1359
01:48:01,152 --> 01:48:03,152
fighting my
girlfriend's dad.

1360
01:48:12,512 --> 01:48:14,512
Oh, God!

1361
01:48:21,632 --> 01:48:23,632
I can't believe that worked!

1362
01:48:59,752 --> 01:49:01,872
Chief, Chief, you're losing altitude.
Get outta there!

1363
01:49:01,872 --> 01:49:03,872
I'm not going home
empty-handed.

1364
01:49:13,632 --> 01:49:15,632
Oh, my God!

1365
01:49:29,792 --> 01:49:31,808
Get out of there!
What are you doing?!

1366
01:49:31,832 --> 01:49:33,832
Please turn,
please turn!

1367
01:51:08,652 --> 01:51:10,652
Hey, Pedro.

1368
01:51:59,062 --> 01:52:01,062
Bingo.

1369
01:52:16,752 --> 01:52:20,192
Your wings... Your
wings are gonna explode!

1370
01:52:28,872 --> 01:52:32,432
- Time to go home, Pete!
- I'm trying to save you!

1371
01:52:49,712 --> 01:52:51,712
No!

1372
01:54:07,044 --> 01:54:09,044
<font color="#ffff00"><u>FOUND</u>
FLYING VULTURE GUY
*SPIDER-MAN</font>

1373
01:54:09,044 --> 01:54:10,511
<font color="#ffff00">PS. SORRY ABOUT YOUR PLANE</font>

1374
01:54:32,392 --> 01:54:36,052
You looked so insane.
The whole... Like, it was just crazy!

1375
01:54:36,142 --> 01:54:38,432
He was just like...

1376
01:54:38,592 --> 01:54:40,592
And you were like...

1377
01:54:40,752 --> 01:54:42,752
And then I just hit him with the...

1378
01:54:42,862 --> 01:54:44,862
It was so...
Oh, my God.

1379
01:54:44,952 --> 01:54:48,952
- And you saved me.
- Awesome.

1380
01:54:55,032 --> 01:54:56,732
Hey, Liz!

1381
01:54:58,442 --> 01:55:00,442
I'm gonna miss you.

1382
01:55:02,452 --> 01:55:04,452
Liz...

1383
01:55:10,872 --> 01:55:12,872
Liz, look, I'm so sorry.

1384
01:55:13,432 --> 01:55:15,952
You say that a lot. What
are you sorry for this time?

1385
01:55:17,602 --> 01:55:19,602
The dance?

1386
01:55:19,702 --> 01:55:22,872
That, was a pretty crappy thing to do.

1387
01:55:23,192 --> 01:55:26,632
Yeah, but... Your Dad. I can't imagine
what you're going through.

1388
01:55:27,482 --> 01:55:29,482
If there's anything
I can do to help...

1389
01:55:29,882 --> 01:55:32,242
I guess we're
moving to Oregon.

1390
01:55:32,632 --> 01:55:35,872
Mom says it's nice
there, so that's cool.

1391
01:55:36,872 --> 01:55:38,382
Anyways,

1392
01:55:38,382 --> 01:55:40,632
Dad doesn't want us
here during the trial, so...

1393
01:55:42,472 --> 01:55:44,472
Liz, I... I...

1394
01:55:45,432 --> 01:55:47,432
Bye, Peter.

1395
01:55:47,942 --> 01:55:51,432
Whatever's going on with
you, I hope you figure it out.

1396
01:56:04,312 --> 01:56:08,422
Congratulations, decathlon
national champions!

1397
01:56:10,572 --> 01:56:12,917
I'm gonna have to put this back
in the trophy case soon, but,

1398
01:56:12,942 --> 01:56:15,336
just for motivation right
now, at this practice.

1399
01:56:15,422 --> 01:56:18,992
I'm a little ahead of the game, but
we will need a new team captain next year.

1400
01:56:19,032 --> 01:56:22,772
So I am appointing Michelle.

1401
01:56:26,542 --> 01:56:29,782
Thank you. My
friends call me "MJ."

1402
01:56:30,182 --> 01:56:32,182
I thought you didn't
have any friends.

1403
01:56:32,412 --> 01:56:34,412
I didn't.

1404
01:56:38,792 --> 01:56:42,042
- I gotta go.
- Hey, where're you going?

1405
01:56:43,562 --> 01:56:45,902
What are you hiding, Peter?

1406
01:56:47,172 --> 01:56:48,828
I'm just kidding.
I don't care. Bye.

1407
01:56:48,852 --> 01:56:50,952
Alright. So, we should
run some drills.

1408
01:56:59,462 --> 01:57:02,862
Hey, Happy. What
are you doing here?

1409
01:57:03,682 --> 01:57:05,682
I really owe you one.

1410
01:57:06,822 --> 01:57:09,192
I don't know what I would
do without this job.

1411
01:57:09,272 --> 01:57:11,272
I mean, before
I met Tony...

1412
01:57:39,532 --> 01:57:41,552
So, how long have
you been here?

1413
01:57:41,572 --> 01:57:43,582
Long enough to be awkward.
Boss wants to see you.

1414
01:57:44,582 --> 01:57:45,848
Is he here, too?

1415
01:57:45,872 --> 01:57:47,872
In the toilet?
No. He's upstate.

1416
01:57:47,892 --> 01:57:49,348
Upstate?
Like upstate, upstate?

1417
01:57:49,372 --> 01:57:50,873
Yeah. Let's go.

1418
01:57:52,212 --> 01:57:55,522
Take a look. It's pretty
impressive, huh?

1419
01:57:56,372 --> 01:57:58,512
They just finished remodelling
the whole thing.

1420
01:58:24,292 --> 01:58:26,432
- You don't see that everyday.
- Oh, there they are.

1421
01:58:27,932 --> 01:58:30,332
- How was the ride out?
- Good.

1422
01:58:30,742 --> 01:58:32,742
Give me a minute
with the kid.

1423
01:58:33,212 --> 01:58:35,212
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

1424
01:58:35,392 --> 01:58:38,482
- I gotta talk to the kid.
- I'll be close behind.

1425
01:58:38,482 --> 01:58:42,062
How about a loose follow, alright?
Boundaries are good.

1426
01:58:46,932 --> 01:58:49,658
Sorry I took your suit.
I mean, you had it coming.

1427
01:58:49,682 --> 01:58:52,992
Actually, it turns out, it was the perfect, sort
of tough love moment that you needed, right?

1428
01:58:52,992 --> 01:58:55,748
To urge you on, right? Wouldn't
you think? Don't you think?

1429
01:58:55,772 --> 01:58:57,772
Let's just say it was.

1430
01:58:59,412 --> 01:59:02,632
- Mr. Stark, I really...
- You screwed the pooch hard, big-time.

1431
01:59:02,882 --> 01:59:04,968
But then, you
did the right thing.

1432
01:59:04,992 --> 01:59:06,622
You took the dog to the free clinic, you...

1433
01:59:06,622 --> 01:59:10,252
Raised the hybrid puppies...
All right, not my best analogy.

1434
01:59:10,972 --> 01:59:12,972
I was wrong
about you.

1435
01:59:13,372 --> 01:59:15,272
I think with a little
more mentoring...

1436
01:59:15,762 --> 01:59:17,762
You could be a real
asset to the team.

1437
01:59:19,732 --> 01:59:21,568
- To the team?
- Yeah. Anyway...

1438
01:59:21,592 --> 01:59:23,412
There's about 50
reporters behind that door.

1439
01:59:23,412 --> 01:59:25,008
Real ones, not bloggers.

1440
01:59:25,132 --> 01:59:29,228
When you're ready...
I want you to try that on.

1441
01:59:29,252 --> 01:59:33,052
And I'll introduce the world to the
newest official member of the Avengers,

1442
01:59:33,132 --> 01:59:35,132
Spider-Man.

1443
01:59:40,172 --> 01:59:42,172
Yeah. Give that a lick.

1444
01:59:47,892 --> 01:59:50,852
So, after the press conference, Happy
will show you to your room, your new quarters.

1445
01:59:50,852 --> 01:59:54,702
- Where's he between? He's next to Vision?
- Yeah, Vision's not big on doors.

1446
01:59:54,778 --> 01:59:55,578
It's fun.

1447
01:59:55,578 --> 01:59:57,578
- Or walls.
- He'll fit right in.

1448
02:00:04,872 --> 02:00:06,872
Thank you, Mr. Stark.

1449
02:00:07,192 --> 02:00:09,192
But, I... I'm good.

1450
02:00:09,352 --> 02:00:11,892
You're good? Good,
how are you good?

1451
02:00:12,252 --> 02:00:16,412
I mean, I'd rather just stay on
the ground, for a little while.

1452
02:00:16,522 --> 02:00:18,522
Friendly, neighborhood Spider-Man.

1453
02:00:18,602 --> 02:00:20,732
Somebody's gotta stick
out for the little guy, right?

1454
02:00:20,932 --> 02:00:24,372
You turning me down?
You better think about this. Look at that.

1455
02:00:24,612 --> 02:00:27,288
Look at me. Last chance,
Yes or No?

1456
02:00:27,612 --> 02:00:29,228
- No.
- Okay.

1457
02:00:29,252 --> 02:00:32,452
It's kind of a Springsteeny,
working class hero, vibe of the day.

1458
02:00:32,472 --> 02:00:34,612
Happy will take you home.

1459
02:00:34,612 --> 02:00:36,208
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

1460
02:00:36,332 --> 02:00:39,692
You mind waiting in the car?
I need a minute.

1461
02:00:39,932 --> 02:00:42,428
- Thank you, Mr. Stark.
- Yes, Mr. Parker. You're very welcome.

1462
02:00:42,452 --> 02:00:44,452
See you around.

1463
02:00:52,312 --> 02:00:55,477
That was a test, right?
There's nobody back there?

1464
02:00:55,502 --> 02:00:58,912
Yes. You passed. All right,
skedaddle there, young buck.

1465
02:00:58,912 --> 02:01:02,572
- Thank you, Mr. Stark. Thank you!
- Yeah. Thank you!

1466
02:01:03,892 --> 02:01:05,892
Told you he's a good kid.

1467
02:01:11,882 --> 02:01:13,288
- Where's the kid?
- He left.

1468
02:01:13,313 --> 02:01:16,162
- Everybody's waiting.
- You know what, he actually made a really mature choice.

1469
02:01:16,362 --> 02:01:19,562
- He just surprised the heck out of us.
- Did you guys screw this up?

1470
02:01:19,562 --> 02:01:22,268
- He told the kid to go wait in the car.
- Are you kidding me?

1471
02:01:22,292 --> 02:01:24,332
I have a room full of people in there,
waiting for some big announcement.

1472
02:01:24,412 --> 02:01:27,852
- What am I gonna tell them?
- Think of something. How about...

1473
02:01:28,452 --> 02:01:30,892
- Happy, do you still got that ring?
- Do I...

1474
02:01:30,892 --> 02:01:34,612
- The engagement ring.
- Are you kidding? I've been carrying this since 2008.

1475
02:01:37,772 --> 02:01:40,808
- Okay.
- I think I can think of something better than that.

1476
02:01:40,832 --> 02:01:42,832
Buy us a little time.

1477
02:01:44,132 --> 02:01:46,132
Like we need time.

1478
02:01:46,252 --> 02:01:49,353
- I can't believe you have that thing in your pocket.
- Can I get the door for you, Hon?

1479
02:02:05,692 --> 02:02:07,692
Hey, May, did you
get dinner already?

1480
02:02:11,600 --> 02:02:15,600
<font color="#ffff00">This Belongs
To You
*TS</font>

1481
02:02:18,092 --> 02:02:20,092
May?

1482
02:02:23,350 --> 02:02:27,794
s u b t i t l e  by

1483
02:02:27,794 --> 02:02:32,238
s u b t i t l e  by
i  m  o  t

1484
02:02:40,642 --> 02:02:42,086
What the fu**!!
